1
00:00:37,913 --> 00:00:43,836
(Man A's ragged breathing)

2
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:45,671
(Man B)
S... stop! Stop it!

3
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:46,756
Aaaah!

4
00:00:49,008 --> 00:00:50,885
(men shouting)

5
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:52,595
(gunfire)

6
00:00:57,516 --> 00:01:00,019
(men and women screaming)

7
00:01:07,943 --> 00:01:10,821
(Chang)
Enough!
Grab that and get out!

8
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:12,323
(Chang) Tch!
(Man A) Chang!

9
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:14,450
(Chang) Just as planned.

10
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:16,577
Hah... hah... hah...

11
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,289
(gunfire)

12
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:21,707
(Man A) Aaaah!

13
00:01:21,832 --> 00:01:24,043
Guh! Ah! Ah!

14
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:06,794
(Officer A)
A high-traffic area detouring around the continental shelf...

15
00:02:07,211 --> 00:02:08,712
(Officer B)
They all look suspicious.

16
00:02:09,505 --> 00:02:12,174
(Navigator A)
It could well be a disguised ship.

17
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:13,008
(Officer A)
Communications?

18
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,719
(Communications Officer)
Ah... The XO has gone to ask the captain...

19
00:02:15,845 --> 00:02:17,263
(XO)
Tell the chief engineer.
(Engineer) Yes, sir!

20
00:02:18,597 --> 00:02:20,516
(Navigator A)
An Anaheim subsidiary, huh...

21
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,101
Hmm...

22
00:02:22,226 --> 00:02:24,228
(Navigator B)
If we're right, a mobile suit will appear...

23
00:02:24,353 --> 00:02:25,563
This ship will sink.

24
00:02:26,272 --> 00:02:28,983
The navy today can't do a thing about it.

25
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:30,150
(XO)
Listen up!

26
00:02:30,276 --> 00:02:33,070
From now on, this ship, like the Halmahera,

27
00:02:33,195 --> 00:02:37,408
will search for fallen colony debris
that could serve as a base.

28
00:02:37,825 --> 00:02:40,536
(Navigator B)
Again?
Just doing the Air Force's bidding, XO?

29
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:42,496
(XO)
Don't say that! It's the captain's decision.

30
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:45,457
(Navigator B)
The captain just doesn't want
the General Staff to come down on him.

31
00:02:45,583 --> 00:02:48,002
(Navigator A)
Shh.

32
00:02:48,127 --> 00:02:48,836
Whoosh.

33
00:02:48,961 --> 00:02:49,920
(Fencer)
What do we do?

34
00:02:50,045 --> 00:02:51,505
(Mechanic)
Keep fanning, keep fanning.

35
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:52,423
(Fencer)
Mm.

36
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:54,925
Heh heh heh.

37
00:02:56,969 --> 00:02:57,887
(Crew D humming)

38
00:02:57,887 --> 00:03:00,222
(Crew D humming)
(Chartchai)
I know that much.

39
00:03:00,347 --> 00:03:03,684
Ah... If we raise power output,
we'll be found out.

40
00:03:03,809 --> 00:03:04,935
It's just as hot for us.

41
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,187
(curtain opens)
(Wedge) How is it?

42
00:03:07,313 --> 00:03:10,441
(Chartchai)
Passive sonar: just one ping five minutes ago.

43
00:03:10,566 --> 00:03:11,567
Communications...

44
00:03:12,151 --> 00:03:13,485
It's not voice, so I can't tell.

45
00:03:13,485 --> 00:03:14,278
It's not voice, so I can't tell.
(Crew C) Captain!

46
00:03:14,403 --> 00:03:16,739
(Crew C)
The submarine is moving away.

47
00:03:16,864 --> 00:03:17,865
(Wedge)
There you have it.

48
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:18,866
(Chartchai)
What about below?

49
00:03:18,991 --> 00:03:23,287
Ah... just in case,
maintain alert for another 10 minutes.

50
00:03:23,412 --> 00:03:27,583
(Chartchai)
Another 10... No, make it 20 minutes of alert.

51
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:30,920
(Wedge) Hmph!
This ship's got luck on its side!

52
00:03:31,045 --> 00:03:31,962
(Crew) Yeah!

53
00:03:32,087 --> 00:03:33,422
(Iram) Captain Wedge?

54
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:36,967
(Wedge) Yeah.

55
00:03:39,762 --> 00:03:42,181
Hey...
Fortune
...

56
00:03:44,725 --> 00:03:45,517
...Sheesh.

57
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:51,815
(Raymond) The ones deployed at Oenpelli
are, in fact—

58
00:03:52,316 --> 00:03:54,443
They're a group unrelated to us.

59
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:55,569
(Hendrix) That's right.

60
00:03:55,694 --> 00:03:58,656
We've been preparing
for the Adelaide Conference.

61
00:03:58,781 --> 00:04:02,826
(Civet) But hey,
they're still part of the anti-Federation movement.

62
00:04:02,952 --> 00:04:03,744
(Ridorick) Agreed.

63
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,913
(Raymond)
I can't ignore it either.

64
00:04:06,038 --> 00:04:09,249
(Kelia) But if we help them,
what do we do afterwards?

65
00:04:09,375 --> 00:04:13,754
(footsteps)

66
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,589
(Wedge) Quack Salver
used to say,

67
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:19,468
"When more people get involved,
things get complicated..."

68
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:21,303
(Raymond and others)
"It only leads to chaos."

69
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:22,888
(laughter)
(Hendrix) ...or something.

70
00:04:23,013 --> 00:04:25,349
(Maximilian)
That's Mafty's catchphrase.

71
00:04:25,474 --> 00:04:28,727
(Iram) More importantly,
covering this entire South Pacific—

72
00:04:28,852 --> 00:04:31,689
Federation mobile suits are deployed.

73
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:35,025
We strike at the Kimberley unit at Oenpelli,

74
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:38,737
and stop the follow-up unit,
the Kirke at Davao, in its tracks.

75
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:41,156
Even stopping the main conference
becomes difficult.

76
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:43,784
...That's Hathaway's thinking.

77
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:45,911
(Kelia) But
if we get bogged down at Kimberley,

78
00:04:46,036 --> 00:04:49,081
reinforcements might come
from Kenneth's unit, right?

79
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:52,418
(Wedge)
That risk is very real.

80
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:58,465
(Golf) Hah... hah... hah...

81
00:04:58,590 --> 00:05:00,843
Hah... hah...

82
00:05:04,096 --> 00:05:07,683
(Golf) According to Emeralda,
she was a real beauty.

83
00:05:08,517 --> 00:05:09,852
(Gawman) I was too far away...

84
00:05:10,894 --> 00:05:12,271
I couldn't tell.

85
00:05:16,108 --> 00:05:18,819
Once more.
We'll keep at it until your body learns.

86
00:05:23,407 --> 00:05:24,992
(Raymond)
If we engage at Oenpelli,

87
00:05:25,534 --> 00:05:27,953
(Raymond) What about magazine resupply?
(Maximilian) No problem.

88
00:05:28,287 --> 00:05:30,372
For the Messers, anyway.

89
00:05:32,207 --> 00:05:35,544
(Iram) So,
to help you decide,

90
00:05:35,669 --> 00:05:39,506
I'd like to explain the upcoming reinforcement points
and supplies.

91
00:05:40,716 --> 00:05:41,675
Take a look.

92
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:50,100
I've had three points set up
on the wall.

93
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:52,352
(Civet)
Are we getting more pilots?

94
00:05:52,478 --> 00:05:53,479
(Iram) I've put in a request.

95
00:05:53,604 --> 00:05:55,230
(Wedge)
What about Mafty?

96
00:05:57,775 --> 00:05:59,485
(Kelia) Fatigue seems to have caught up with him.

97
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:01,653
I've laid him down.

98
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:36,438
(Crewman A) The enemy spy—
that's about Hathaway's woman, right?

99
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:39,024
(Crewman B)
They spent the night in the same room.

100
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:41,235
You expect me to believe nothing happened?

101
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:43,237
(Crew A) Huh? No way.
(Crew B) Right?

102
00:06:43,362 --> 00:06:45,531
(crew laughter)

103
00:06:45,656 --> 00:06:46,573
(sound of door closing)

104
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:51,370
(Quess) You sensed something, didn't you?
Hathaway

105
00:06:51,495 --> 00:06:52,371
(Hathaway) Yeah...

106
00:06:54,081 --> 00:06:56,166
(Quess)
I wonder if he's still in Davao.

107
00:06:57,209 --> 00:06:59,586
(Hathaway) This is
about how to handle Gigi inside me.

108
00:06:59,711 --> 00:07:02,214
It's just a matter of deciding.

109
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:47,801
Hathaway Noah, huh...

110
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:50,304
(sound of Big Carrier's flight)

111
00:07:53,557 --> 00:07:55,851
(Gigi) Kenneth is on the move too...

112
00:07:57,311 --> 00:08:00,689
Let's change plans...
We'd better hurry.

113
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:08,488
Is this the only channel?

114
00:08:10,324 --> 00:08:12,034
(Maid) It's different from space.

115
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:14,703
This is one of the better places.

116
00:08:15,078 --> 00:08:16,830
Even though it's a fine night tonight.

117
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:18,498
Are you all alone?

118
00:08:21,585 --> 00:08:23,670
(Cardeas) Most lives are

119
00:08:23,795 --> 00:08:25,756
for the sake of one day's joy,

120
00:08:25,881 --> 00:08:28,383
there are 365 days of patience.

121
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:33,472
(Gigi) What do you do?

122
00:08:33,597 --> 00:08:38,185
(Cardeas) Someday, when you face
an unimaginable situation

123
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:40,771
so you won't make the wrong decision,

124
00:08:40,896 --> 00:08:44,775
you have to obtain
some information beforehand.

125
00:08:45,484 --> 00:08:46,693
Gigi.

126
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:49,655
If you have one truly good day,

127
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:52,824
you can endure a year of loneliness.

128
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:53,784
(Gigi) Mm...

129
00:08:55,661 --> 00:08:58,789
(Cardeas)
That's what human life is like.

130
00:09:07,089 --> 00:09:10,801
(female newscaster) The conference will be held
for three days starting on the 26th.

131
00:09:10,926 --> 00:09:13,971
Since it's the first time in 13 years
that it's being held on Earth,

132
00:09:14,096 --> 00:09:17,349
speculation that the government
may make some kind of announcement

133
00:09:17,474 --> 00:09:18,517
is growing.

134
00:09:18,642 --> 00:09:21,770
Along with this,
the newly appointed Commander Kenneth

135
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:24,064
is also drawing attention, it seems.

136
00:09:25,190 --> 00:09:28,986
Now let's hear from reporter Lyle,
who covered the press conference.

137
00:09:29,111 --> 00:09:31,822
(Lyle) With the arrival of the new commander,
Colonel Kenneth Sleg,

138
00:09:31,947 --> 00:09:33,740
the Earth Federation Forces stationed in Davao

139
00:09:33,865 --> 00:09:35,867
from Kimberley Unit
to Kirke Unit

140
00:09:35,993 --> 00:09:36,243
announced that it would change its designation.

141
00:09:36,243 --> 00:09:38,370
announced that it would change its designation.
(Gigi) I know that...

142
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:40,872
(Gigi)
Everyone's keeping it a secret...
(Analyst) The new commander's arrival

143
00:09:40,998 --> 00:09:41,290
(sound of Big Carrier's flight)

144
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:44,459
(sound of Big Carrier's flight)
This can be seen as a move aimed at
the upcoming Adelaide Conference.

145
00:09:44,459 --> 00:09:45,085
(sound of Big Carrier's flight)

146
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:46,545
(sound of Big Carrier's flight)
Concern over holding it on Earth,
where anti-Federation organizations are active—

147
00:09:46,545 --> 00:09:49,381
Concern over holding it on Earth,
where anti-Federation organizations are active—

148
00:09:49,506 --> 00:09:52,092
To also suppress the voices of Federation lawmakers,

149
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:56,054
the stability of the Federation Forces in Oceania
is required.

150
00:09:56,888 --> 00:09:58,432
(Intelligence Officer B)
Water depth exceeds 6,000 meters.

151
00:09:58,557 --> 00:10:00,809
Early retrieval appears difficult.

152
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:01,727
(Minecche) Next!

153
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:05,272
(Kenneth) Mafty's base?

154
00:10:07,649 --> 00:10:09,276
(Intelligence Officer B) Today at 0808 hours.

155
00:10:09,401 --> 00:10:13,030
The 7th Fighter-Attack Squadron found it and landed.

156
00:10:13,155 --> 00:10:14,990
What Mafty calls the 'tree' of Rodoiseya—

157
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:16,074
It appears to be one of their bases...

158
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:16,950
It appears to be one of their bases...
(Kenneth) And?

159
00:10:17,409 --> 00:10:18,910
(Intelligence Officer B) The interior was completely empty.

160
00:10:19,036 --> 00:10:21,705
We're expanding the search area to a 300-kilometer radius...

161
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:25,292
Threaten the Navy if you must—make them search for the other bases.

162
00:10:25,667 --> 00:10:27,836
By order of the Joint Chiefs of Staff!

163
00:10:27,961 --> 00:10:29,296
(Intelligence Officer B) Yes, sir.
(Kenneth) Next!

164
00:10:29,421 --> 00:10:30,797
(Intelligence Officer C) Here are the images of the craft.

165
00:10:31,173 --> 00:10:32,174
(controls beep)

166
00:10:33,508 --> 00:10:35,010
(Kenneth) A Gundam imitation...

167
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:39,139
(Intelligence Officer C)
We processed it, but this is the best we can do.

168
00:10:39,264 --> 00:10:41,641
A unit they protected even at the cost of abandoning one of their bases.

169
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:46,605
So we must consider it a combat capability on par with the Penelope.

170
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:47,522
(Intelligence Officer C) Yes, sir.

171
00:10:49,066 --> 00:10:51,943
I want to review Adelaide's defense system.

172
00:10:52,069 --> 00:10:53,403
Where is Lieutenant Colonel Mainzer?

173
00:10:53,528 --> 00:10:54,946
(Minecche) I've called for him.

174
00:10:55,781 --> 00:10:56,823
(Intelligence Officer C) Colonel Kenneth.

175
00:10:58,408 --> 00:10:59,951
(Kenneth)
What about the records from Lane's submerged unit?

176
00:11:00,077 --> 00:11:01,828
(Intelligence Officer C) Recovery will take about two weeks...

177
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:04,664
(Kenneth) Three days.
Have it ready before the conference.

178
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:06,625
Your career is on the line.

179
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:07,626
(Intelligence Officer C) Yes, sir.

180
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:11,421
(Minecche)
As expected, it's Anaheim?

181
00:11:11,546 --> 00:11:12,714
(Kenneth) Most likely.

182
00:11:13,006 --> 00:11:16,051
(Minecche)
Regarding Lieutenant Lane's use of the experimental model.

183
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:17,511
It was approved, then.

184
00:11:17,636 --> 00:11:19,805
Yeah, by the conference, he—

185
00:11:19,930 --> 00:11:22,057
He must become a combat asset.

186
00:11:22,057 --> 00:11:22,933
He must become a combat asset.
(Lagoid) Please wait just a little longer!

187
00:11:22,933 --> 00:11:24,017
(Lagoid)
Please wait just a little longer!

188
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:26,186
(Lagoid)
He has arrived!

189
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,986
Director Hundley Yeoksan

190
00:11:43,537 --> 00:11:44,621
(Maintenance Crew C) Where are you going?

191
00:11:44,746 --> 00:11:47,416
(Maintenance Crew D) At this hour, nothing's open.

192
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:50,001
(Mechanic)
Flight units five and eight—

193
00:11:50,127 --> 00:11:51,920
We're rebuilding them with brand-new cores!

194
00:11:52,421 --> 00:11:53,463
Hurry up!

195
00:11:57,342 --> 00:11:58,718
Don't worry.

196
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:02,264
It'll have to be transported, but we'll make it in time for the conference.

197
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:07,686
Until then, please make do with the Aryuzeus.

198
00:12:08,145 --> 00:12:09,604
(Lane) Sorry for the trouble.

199
00:12:16,528 --> 00:12:18,530
(Lane, voiceover) That was because of Kenneth's orders.

200
00:12:18,655 --> 00:12:21,450
It was the guilt of having used a hostage.

201
00:12:23,577 --> 00:12:24,244
(Lane) Agh!

202
00:12:24,369 --> 00:12:27,247
(Kenneth) Listen up!
There's no room for honor.

203
00:12:27,956 --> 00:12:29,791
The ones who win
become justice.

204
00:12:30,292 --> 00:12:31,585
Burn that into your heart!!

205
00:12:32,043 --> 00:12:33,462
Lane Aim!!

206
00:12:35,297 --> 00:12:38,592
I won't be beaten
by a Gundam wannabe again...

207
00:12:38,717 --> 00:12:40,135
Or by those adults...

208
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:59,446
(Yeoksan)
Lieutenant Lane Aim, wasn't it?

209
00:12:59,863 --> 00:13:02,282
You want me to help
round up illegal residents?

210
00:13:05,410 --> 00:13:09,372
(Yeoksan) Over a single prisoner,
the man tasked with defending the Cabinet Council—

211
00:13:09,498 --> 00:13:11,875
I have no intention
of dragging you down.

212
00:13:16,004 --> 00:13:19,883
Even I, when it comes to the Federation government's
recent attitude toward Earth management—

213
00:13:20,008 --> 00:13:22,260
do not necessarily agree with it.

214
00:13:22,385 --> 00:13:25,055
(Kenneth)
The head of Man Hunter...
How dare you!

215
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,699
(Kelia) Did you take your medicine?

216
00:13:46,618 --> 00:13:49,746
(Hathaway) It makes my head all foggy,
so I don't want to take it.

217
00:13:51,998 --> 00:13:53,208
(Kelia) Are you really going out?

218
00:13:54,459 --> 00:13:56,253
What Kimberley is doing
in Oenpelli—

219
00:13:56,378 --> 00:13:58,255
I have to confirm it.

220
00:13:59,089 --> 00:14:01,675
It might be useful for our future activities.

221
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,886
(Kelia)
Your head is full of nothing but ideology...

222
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:07,847
That's exactly why they've
put you up as Mafty.

223
00:14:07,973 --> 00:14:09,474
You do realize that, right?

224
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:12,185
It's something
someone has to do.

225
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:14,563
For a powerless organization,
there's no other way.

226
00:14:14,688 --> 00:14:16,648
So the organization is to blame?

227
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:19,150
(Hathaway)
Right now, this is all I can manage.

228
00:14:19,943 --> 00:14:21,861
You of all people should understand.

229
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:24,948
You should just take it...

230
00:14:25,699 --> 00:14:27,576
(eating sounds)

231
00:14:27,701 --> 00:14:28,618
(Hathaway) Mm...

232
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,789
(Hathaway) Mm... mmm...

233
00:14:32,914 --> 00:14:37,252
(eating sounds)

234
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:46,303
(Mihessia)
It was originally "Oenpelli",

235
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:49,723
but after some official messed up,
the "p" became a "b".

236
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:50,640
(Emeralda) Huh.

237
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:53,226
(Golf)
What the hell? It's packed.

238
00:14:59,733 --> 00:15:01,067
(Lulu)
...So what's the deal?

239
00:15:01,484 --> 00:15:02,611
(Emeralda) I don't know.

240
00:15:02,736 --> 00:15:05,155
(Betchy)
Word is, it ended ages ago.

241
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,364
(Hala) Really?

242
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:09,117
(hair clipper buzzing)

243
00:15:10,201 --> 00:15:11,995
(Mihessia)
That was a move to figure out

244
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,913
who she really was.

245
00:15:14,039 --> 00:15:16,958
(Golf)
You're the only one who believes that.

246
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:18,501
(Emeralda) Don't "you" me!

247
00:15:18,627 --> 00:15:21,921
(Hala)
So you're saying he had no choice but
to say that, given his position?

248
00:15:22,047 --> 00:15:24,007
(Golf)
Pretty much.

249
00:15:45,236 --> 00:15:46,613
(Mihessia) Hm? Oh!

250
00:15:50,325 --> 00:15:51,451
Sorry!

251
00:15:51,576 --> 00:15:52,369
(Hathaway) It's below.

252
00:15:52,494 --> 00:15:53,411
(Mihessia) Yes!

253
00:15:57,707 --> 00:15:59,834
What about Oenpelli?

254
00:16:00,168 --> 00:16:01,795
(Hathaway)
What do you think, Mihessia?

255
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,339
As General Quack is also pleased,

256
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:07,884
and to build momentum for the anti-Federation movement,

257
00:16:08,009 --> 00:16:11,179
I believe they are a group we must value.

258
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:12,889
You're saying we shouldn't ignore them?

259
00:16:13,014 --> 00:16:16,184
(Mihessia)
No, it's a difficult call.

260
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:18,812
And we've also received word
about the conference venue change...

261
00:16:18,937 --> 00:16:21,314
(Mechanic C) Is the I-field's shape collapsing?

262
00:16:21,439 --> 00:16:22,232
(Member E) Hmm...

263
00:16:22,232 --> 00:16:23,191
(Member E) Hmm...
(Maximilian)
Try restarting it again.

264
00:16:23,191 --> 00:16:24,275
(Maximilian)
Try restarting it again.

265
00:16:24,401 --> 00:16:25,819
If not, we'll swap it with the Byno.

266
00:16:25,944 --> 00:16:27,362
(Mechanic B) Got it.
(Hathaway) What's wrong?

267
00:16:27,487 --> 00:16:30,323
(Member E) The main engine's I-field isn't working properly,

268
00:16:30,699 --> 00:16:32,826
so it forces a shutdown.

269
00:16:33,368 --> 00:16:34,160
(Maximilian) Hm...

270
00:16:36,621 --> 00:16:37,956
(Mihessia) What do you mean?

271
00:16:38,081 --> 00:16:41,960
(Hathaway) That's called a Minovsky-
Ionesco type thermonuclear reactor.

272
00:16:42,085 --> 00:16:45,004
By using the I-field for electromagnetic induction
inside the reactor,

273
00:16:45,130 --> 00:16:47,465
it stabilizes the plasma.

274
00:16:47,590 --> 00:16:49,175
(Member E)
At the same time, the I-field

275
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:51,970
confines high-speed neutrons inside the reactor.

276
00:16:52,095 --> 00:16:54,305
(Mihessia) So that's why it shuts down...

277
00:16:54,431 --> 00:16:56,641
Then without Minovsky particles,

278
00:16:56,766 --> 00:16:58,643
mobile suits can't operate?

279
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:01,062
Well, that's about right.

280
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:02,731
I learned something!

281
00:17:03,648 --> 00:17:06,651
(Member E) The central density of the potential well
is dropping, right?

282
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:08,570
the Coulomb barrier's
tunnel-effect area

283
00:17:08,695 --> 00:17:09,237
hasn't been reached.

284
00:17:09,237 --> 00:17:10,071
It hasn't been reached.
(Hathaway)
What about Gawman?

285
00:17:11,156 --> 00:17:12,240
(Maximilian)
There's an M-Messer at Sealac,

286
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:14,033
so he went to take a look.

287
00:17:15,118 --> 00:17:18,496
(Betchy) Whoa! Hahaha!
(Gawman) Hahaha! Whoa!

288
00:17:19,831 --> 00:17:23,209
(Hathaway) The M-type throttle quirk
hasn't been fixed, right?

289
00:17:23,585 --> 00:17:25,754
(Maximilian)
Because Eme won't give it up!

290
00:17:25,879 --> 00:17:27,005
(Hathaway) Hmm...

291
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:30,759
(Maximilian)
Hathaway, about Oenpelli...

292
00:17:30,884 --> 00:17:32,427
(Hathaway)
Are you also in the stay camp?

293
00:17:32,552 --> 00:17:35,930
No, the missile cargo recovery rate
is low.

294
00:17:37,098 --> 00:17:41,060
Considering the operation, we can't use funnel missiles.

295
00:17:41,311 --> 00:17:42,103
I see...

296
00:17:42,771 --> 00:17:44,397
You've heard from Kelia, haven't you?

297
00:17:45,148 --> 00:17:46,065
(Hathaway) Yeah...

298
00:17:48,985 --> 00:17:49,819
I'll keep that in mind.

299
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:05,877
(Hathaway) What about Oenpelli?

300
00:18:07,170 --> 00:18:08,713
(Josef) No change.

301
00:18:09,047 --> 00:18:10,840
(Chartchai)
Weren't they wiped out?

302
00:18:10,965 --> 00:18:12,258
It's not that simple.

303
00:18:12,884 --> 00:18:15,678
It could just be that their radio was hit.

304
00:18:15,804 --> 00:18:18,473
(Josef)
It's still serious either way.

305
00:18:18,765 --> 00:18:20,558
(Chartchai)
And then there's this.

306
00:18:20,683 --> 00:18:23,478
The radio traffic from Davao
to Guangzhou and Hong Kong

307
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:25,522
The problem is, it's been increasing.

308
00:18:25,647 --> 00:18:29,859
An order to gather ground troops
and police in Guangzhou, right?

309
00:18:30,443 --> 00:18:34,322
(Hathaway)
Guangzhou...
The Federation cabinet ministers like it there.

310
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:36,449
(Chartchai)
Iram says it's staged too.

311
00:18:37,617 --> 00:18:41,704
It could be made to look like
the conference is being moved from Adelaide, but...

312
00:18:41,830 --> 00:18:43,122
It's too obvious.

313
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:46,501
(Crew D)
The captain's saying
the same kind of thing, y'know.

314
00:18:46,626 --> 00:18:49,712
Either way, we're sortieing.
Keep intercepting their communications.

315
00:18:49,838 --> 00:18:52,674
(Chartchai)
So all of this is a diversion?

316
00:18:54,509 --> 00:18:56,761
(Maximilian)
Xi
will be brought up first.

317
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:57,804
(Hathaway)
So it can launch?

318
00:18:57,929 --> 00:19:00,890
(Maximilian)
Yeah. Head up to the aft deck.

319
00:19:01,516 --> 00:19:03,643
(Hathaway)
What about the barrier capability check?

320
00:19:03,768 --> 00:19:05,061
Leave it to Julia.

321
00:19:21,202 --> 00:19:22,328
(Hathaway) Mm...

322
00:19:25,456 --> 00:19:26,499
(Kelia) Oh...

323
00:19:30,086 --> 00:19:31,754
(Kelia) Hathaway!
(Hathaway) What?

324
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,924
(Kelia) What...? It's nothing.

325
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:38,136
(Hathaway)
You, of all people, should understand.

326
00:19:38,261 --> 00:19:41,556
(Kelia) What happened?
With that girl... Gigi, or whatever her name is.

327
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:45,143
(Hathaway)
I came into contact with a dangerous girl.

328
00:19:45,268 --> 00:19:46,853
And I couldn't eliminate her.

329
00:19:47,395 --> 00:19:49,355
I had no choice but to board the Xi.

330
00:19:49,898 --> 00:19:51,316
That's what's eating at me.

331
00:19:51,733 --> 00:19:53,443
(Kelia) I heard that.

332
00:19:54,319 --> 00:19:55,862
(Hathaway) It's the truth.

333
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:59,991
(Kelia) Yes, I know
you wouldn't lie.

334
00:20:00,116 --> 00:20:02,744
Besides...
probabilistically speaking...

335
00:20:02,869 --> 00:20:05,079
You can get by without lying, can't you?

336
00:20:06,664 --> 00:20:07,874
(Hathaway) Hah...

337
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:11,586
Hathaway!

338
00:20:12,545 --> 00:20:13,838
Have you started hating me?

339
00:20:15,048 --> 00:20:18,509
This isn't something
that can be reduced to like or hate.

340
00:20:18,635 --> 00:20:21,888
But...
when you come at me like that...

341
00:20:29,771 --> 00:20:30,688
(Kelia) Hathaway...!

342
00:20:31,147 --> 00:20:34,192
Sorry. Let me work for now.

343
00:20:34,317 --> 00:20:36,778
(Kelia)
You made this work for yourself...!

344
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,543
Then you do it.

345
00:20:52,669 --> 00:20:53,920
(Crew) Huh? What do we do?

346
00:21:00,677 --> 00:21:02,303
(Wedge) Hm... Tch...

347
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:06,849
We're supposed to reach Oenpelli
by sunset, aren't we?

348
00:21:06,975 --> 00:21:09,519
(Raymond) What's the status
on the assault team's boarding?

349
00:21:09,644 --> 00:21:10,979
(Mihessia) From Sealuck!

350
00:21:11,104 --> 00:21:13,439
The Galcezon's launch
looks OK.

351
00:21:13,564 --> 00:21:15,358
(Wedge)
Where's Hathaway's Gundam?

352
00:21:16,442 --> 00:21:19,612
(Iram) Hathaway!
Launch the Kirke unit!

353
00:21:20,405 --> 00:21:23,866
(Hathaway) Go ahead!
Julia's on edge!

354
00:21:24,409 --> 00:21:25,201
(Iram) Captain!

355
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:26,953
(Wedge) Do it!

356
00:21:27,078 --> 00:21:30,498
If we keep dawdling,
reinforcements from Davao will show up!

357
00:21:34,961 --> 00:21:37,797
(Civet)
How's the M-type treating you?

358
00:21:37,922 --> 00:21:40,425
It's still got a lot of quirks, but

359
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:42,719
Just right for an old-timer.

360
00:21:42,844 --> 00:21:43,970
Launch, Civet!

361
00:21:44,095 --> 00:21:45,471
Hey!

362
00:21:45,596 --> 00:21:48,057
Second Galcezon, launching!

363
00:21:52,395 --> 00:21:59,360
(Civet and the others whoop)

364
00:22:00,236 --> 00:22:03,031
(Wedge)
Those damn brats!

365
00:22:03,406 --> 00:22:05,033
(Raymond) Iram!
The first one's good to go!

366
00:22:06,117 --> 00:22:07,118
(Iram) Roger.

367
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:11,414
Captain, Iram and I
talked it over, but...

368
00:22:11,956 --> 00:22:14,292
(Raymond)
First Galcezon, launching!

369
00:22:15,918 --> 00:22:17,754
(Hathaway)
Julia! Hurry!

370
00:22:17,879 --> 00:22:19,130
(Julia) I know.

371
00:22:19,672 --> 00:22:20,923
It's almost done!

372
00:22:21,924 --> 00:22:24,927
(Hathaway) Ah...
I told you to at least put on a T-shirt.

373
00:22:25,053 --> 00:22:26,179
(Julia) More importantly—

374
00:22:26,596 --> 00:22:28,806
What's with this reckless plan?

375
00:22:28,931 --> 00:22:31,309
I can't agree with the assault team selection either!

376
00:22:31,309 --> 00:22:31,976
I can't agree with the assault team selection either!
(Hathaway) You think?

377
00:22:31,976 --> 00:22:32,393
(Hathaway) You think?

378
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:34,812
Mihessia's read on people
is pretty sharp.

379
00:22:34,937 --> 00:22:36,731
(Julia)
But still, Kimberley...

380
00:22:36,856 --> 00:22:39,233
They're trained soldiers...

381
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:40,359
Look.

382
00:22:40,485 --> 00:22:43,029
(Hathaway)
Yeah... I know, but

383
00:22:43,154 --> 00:22:46,032
Put something on so those lovely breasts don't get hurt!

384
00:22:46,157 --> 00:22:48,993
(Julia) Only men get
to go topless.

385
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:52,622
We didn't used to wear these
either, back in the day.

386
00:22:55,875 --> 00:22:56,667
(Julia) Hmph!
(Crew) Pfft!

387
00:23:06,594 --> 00:23:07,804
Hathaway!
You're
going to fall!

388
00:23:19,816 --> 00:23:21,275
(Hathaway) Aaaah!

389
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:26,405
♪~

390
00:23:33,955 --> 00:23:35,665
♪ I'll touch that fire for you

391
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:39,085
♪ I do that 3, 4, times again
    I testify for you

392
00:23:39,210 --> 00:23:41,420
♪ I told that lie
    I'd kill that bitch, I do what

393
00:23:41,546 --> 00:23:44,715
♪ All of them around you
    scared to do I'm not

394
00:23:44,841 --> 00:23:48,052
♪ Long as you juggin out here
    for me I got it

395
00:23:48,177 --> 00:23:51,430
♪ Mobbin scheming looting
    hide your bodies

396
00:23:51,556 --> 00:23:54,851
♪ Long as you dreaming about me
    ain't no problem

397
00:23:54,976 --> 00:23:57,937
♪ I don't got nobody
    just with you right now

398
00:23:58,062 --> 00:24:00,273
♪ To tell the truth
    I look better under you

399
00:24:00,398 --> 00:24:06,612
♪ I can't lose when I'm with you

400
00:24:06,737 --> 00:24:09,699
♪ How can I snooze
    and miss the moment

401
00:24:09,824 --> 00:24:11,367
♪ You just too important

402
00:24:11,492 --> 00:24:13,786
♪ Nobody do body like you do

403
00:24:13,911 --> 00:24:19,917
♪ I can't lose when I'm with you

404
00:24:20,042 --> 00:24:23,171
♪ I can't just snooze
  and miss the moment

405
00:24:23,296 --> 00:24:24,881
♪ You just too important

406
00:24:25,006 --> 00:24:28,467
♪ Nobody do body like you do you do

407
00:24:28,593 --> 00:24:29,886
♪ Main one, riding

408
00:24:30,011 --> 00:24:33,264
♪ How you fronting on me
  and I'm the main one trying?

409
00:24:33,389 --> 00:24:36,601
♪ How you blame it on me
  and you the main one lying?

410
00:24:36,726 --> 00:24:40,104
♪ How you threatening to leave
  and I'm the main one crying?

411
00:24:40,229 --> 00:24:41,898
♪ Just trying to be your everything

412
00:24:42,023 --> 00:24:46,736
♪ I can lose, oh

413
00:24:47,904 --> 00:24:50,406
♪ I think I know, ooh-woah

414
00:24:57,580 --> 00:24:58,247
(incoming transmission beep)

415
00:24:58,372 --> 00:25:00,791
(Maximilian) The unit's barrier capability
seems fine.

416
00:25:01,250 --> 00:25:03,169
Releasing the line.

417
00:25:03,294 --> 00:25:04,295
(Hathaway) Right.

418
00:25:11,594 --> 00:25:12,386
Hah...

419
00:25:17,558 --> 00:25:19,644
Hah... hah...

420
00:25:44,669 --> 00:25:47,797
This is a mission we might not come back from.

421
00:25:49,048 --> 00:25:50,591
(Iram) We're almost there, aren't we?

422
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:52,718
You call that talking it over with me?

423
00:25:56,597 --> 00:25:59,642
We've come this far
together, haven't we?

424
00:26:01,352 --> 00:26:02,770
So you really are in love.

425
00:26:02,895 --> 00:26:04,522
(Kelia) Stop it.

426
00:26:04,647 --> 00:26:05,523
(Iram) Fine.

427
00:26:06,899 --> 00:26:09,068
I'll see it through to the end
even if I'm alone.

428
00:26:09,443 --> 00:26:10,861
(Kelia) Take care.

429
00:26:11,362 --> 00:26:13,197
(Iram) Huh?
(Kelia) That girl, Gigi...

430
00:26:13,489 --> 00:26:15,741
(Kelia) She might erase Quess.

431
00:26:17,451 --> 00:26:18,911
I have a feeling.

432
00:26:20,538 --> 00:26:21,622
Hah...

433
00:26:29,213 --> 00:26:32,842
(Hathaway, voiceover) At this rate,
I'll become a thoroughly selfish man.

434
00:26:32,967 --> 00:26:37,346
(Hathaway, voiceover) But I will definitely
see Gigi Andalusia again.

435
00:26:37,805 --> 00:26:40,099
(Hathaway, voiceover) Until then,
I can't afford to be careless.

436
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:02,121
(Iram) Even if Kimberley anticipates
our support,

437
00:27:02,246 --> 00:27:05,583
an incursion from this bearing
is a route they won't expect.

438
00:27:06,667 --> 00:27:10,129
The enemy will likely figure we'll use
the mountains east of Oenpelli as cover,

439
00:27:10,254 --> 00:27:12,381
and approach.

440
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:16,552
We'll cross 200 kilometers of sea
in just under ten minutes, then enter the wetlands.

441
00:27:16,677 --> 00:27:19,889
Oenpelli lies tens of kilometers
inland from the coast, but

442
00:27:20,014 --> 00:27:22,058
it's practically at sea level.

443
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:25,311
It's also a dangerous approach bearing
with long sightlines.

444
00:27:25,770 --> 00:27:26,562
(Hathaway) Recon.

445
00:27:26,687 --> 00:27:27,813
(Raymond and others) Roger.

446
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:30,191
(Hathaway) It's Oenpelli.

447
00:27:31,275 --> 00:27:32,818
(alarm)

448
00:27:34,528 --> 00:27:35,321
(Hathaway) Kimberley...!

449
00:27:40,159 --> 00:27:40,951
(alarm)

450
00:27:59,345 --> 00:28:00,388
(Raymond)
Golf's feed is in.

451
00:28:00,846 --> 00:28:01,889
Betchy

452
00:28:03,015 --> 00:28:05,101
(Betchy) Whoa... This is...

453
00:28:06,977 --> 00:28:09,146
(Raymond)
The private army's been wiped out, it seems.

454
00:28:09,271 --> 00:28:10,773
(Hathaway) Is this a corpse?

455
00:28:10,898 --> 00:28:12,858
(Emeralda)
What else could it be?

456
00:28:12,983 --> 00:28:14,068
(Raymond) Damn Kimberley.

457
00:28:14,193 --> 00:28:15,945
He's rattled
because Kenneth showed up.

458
00:28:16,070 --> 00:28:19,407
(Gawman) Hey!
This one's moving toward Jabiru...

459
00:28:19,532 --> 00:28:20,741
(Hathaway) Yeah...

460
00:28:20,866 --> 00:28:22,910
So that's the self-proclaimed Mafty army.

461
00:28:23,035 --> 00:28:25,037
(Civet)
They still have troops left?

462
00:28:25,162 --> 00:28:27,123
(Raymond) The number Kimberley beat to death—

463
00:28:27,248 --> 00:28:29,083
In the thousands, I'd say.

464
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:30,459
(Hala) Are you sure?

465
00:28:30,584 --> 00:28:31,710
(Raymond) Even at the camps outside the city,

466
00:28:31,836 --> 00:28:33,963
there are corpses strewn about
by the hundreds.

467
00:28:34,088 --> 00:28:37,258
(Hathaway) Understood, but
this will be a head-on fight!

468
00:28:37,383 --> 00:28:38,968
(Gawman) That's what we came here for!

469
00:28:39,093 --> 00:28:40,261
(Golf) It's all good!

470
00:28:40,386 --> 00:28:41,637
(Civet) We'll show them.

471
00:28:41,762 --> 00:28:43,806
(Hathaway) It'll be rough.
This is no sneak attack, you know.

472
00:28:43,931 --> 00:28:45,558
(Fencer) A head-on fight's just fine!

473
00:28:45,683 --> 00:28:49,103
(Golf and the others shout)

474
00:28:52,690 --> 00:28:54,358
(Gawman)
Here we go, Hathaway!

475
00:28:59,405 --> 00:29:00,531
(impact sound)
(Pilot) Whoa!

476
00:29:21,844 --> 00:29:22,636
(Hathaway) Are they running?

477
00:29:25,014 --> 00:29:26,140
(explosion)

478
00:29:29,643 --> 00:29:30,853
(alarm)

479
00:29:47,495 --> 00:29:48,120
(incoming transmission beep)

480
00:29:48,245 --> 00:29:50,039
(Gawman)
We're going after the Oenpelli forces!

481
00:29:50,164 --> 00:29:51,332
(Hathaway) Go after them!

482
00:29:51,457 --> 00:29:52,917
Hala, put out the fire!

483
00:29:53,042 --> 00:29:53,834
(Hala) Roger.

484
00:29:53,959 --> 00:29:55,503
(Hathaway) Move and I'll burn you with a beam.

485
00:29:55,628 --> 00:29:58,839
After what you've done,
you have no right to complain!

486
00:30:07,097 --> 00:30:09,099
(Hathaway) This was
one-sided, wasn't it?

487
00:30:13,395 --> 00:30:15,314
Everything's gone mad.

488
00:30:15,439 --> 00:30:16,232
(incoming transmission beep)

489
00:30:16,357 --> 00:30:18,776
(Raymond) Hathaway,
we've located the enemy hideout.

490
00:30:23,906 --> 00:30:24,949
(Betchy) Over there!

491
00:30:25,074 --> 00:30:25,950
(Hathaway) Yeah!

492
00:30:26,909 --> 00:30:28,619
(Hathaway) What's inside?
(Rod) Clear.

493
00:30:29,328 --> 00:30:32,623
(Rod) The Federation administrative staff
and mechanics who were inside—

494
00:30:32,748 --> 00:30:34,333
They've surrendered.

495
00:30:36,502 --> 00:30:37,795
(Hathaway) What about the food supplies?

496
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:39,588
(Rod) They're all gone.

497
00:30:40,714 --> 00:30:42,758
It reeks, doesn't it?

498
00:30:43,926 --> 00:30:45,844
There were prisoners here, see?

499
00:30:47,721 --> 00:30:50,099
Looks like they were beaten pretty badly.

500
00:30:51,725 --> 00:30:53,143
(Hathaway) Torture...

501
00:30:53,269 --> 00:30:54,645
(Emeralda)
Is Hathaway here?

502
00:30:55,104 --> 00:30:56,063
(Hathaway)
I'm here!

503
00:30:57,982 --> 00:30:59,191
(Mechanic A)
Come this way.

504
00:31:00,401 --> 00:31:01,193
(Hathaway)
Yeah...

505
00:31:01,318 --> 00:31:04,446
(Rod)
Apparently someone's still alive in the back.

506
00:31:04,572 --> 00:31:05,614
(Hathaway)
I see...

507
00:31:05,990 --> 00:31:07,199
(Hala)
I'll grab some water.

508
00:31:07,324 --> 00:31:08,158
(Emeralda)
Please.

509
00:31:09,118 --> 00:31:09,910
(Hathaway)
A woman?

510
00:31:10,369 --> 00:31:12,746
(Emeralda)
Yeah. She's in terrible shape.

511
00:31:13,789 --> 00:31:16,417
Even if she survives, she might kill herself.

512
00:31:17,876 --> 00:31:19,712
(Hathaway)
What's the situation here?

513
00:31:19,837 --> 00:31:22,214
(Emeralda)
Hala, explain it to him.

514
00:31:26,010 --> 00:31:29,638
(Hala)
This floor appears to have been used
to hold prisoners.

515
00:31:29,763 --> 00:31:31,473
She's the only survivor.

516
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:35,978
There are over thirty bodies, just from what we've confirmed.

517
00:31:36,103 --> 00:31:37,021
(Hathaway)
What about the Federation troops?

518
00:31:37,146 --> 00:31:38,314
(Hala)
They're on the floor above.

519
00:31:38,439 --> 00:31:41,692
It looks like they came in from the rooftop
in Gustav Karls.

520
00:31:42,401 --> 00:31:44,653
(Hathaway)
Let's bring them here as prisoners.

521
00:31:44,778 --> 00:31:45,654
(Hala)
What?!

522
00:31:45,779 --> 00:31:48,407
(Hathaway)
We have to do at least that, don't we?

523
00:31:49,074 --> 00:31:50,576
It's unpleasant, but...

524
00:31:54,079 --> 00:31:55,956
(Gigi)
I want to go to Hong Kong early tomorrow.

525
00:31:56,081 --> 00:31:57,207
Is there a flight?

526
00:31:57,333 --> 00:31:59,918
(Kenneth)
What? You're leaving already?

527
00:32:00,044 --> 00:32:02,463
(Gigi)
I have work too, you know.

528
00:32:02,588 --> 00:32:06,008
I want to settle things for the Count.

529
00:32:06,133 --> 00:32:07,718
That way, I might be able to...

530
00:32:07,843 --> 00:32:09,970
come back here again.

531
00:32:09,970 --> 00:32:10,512
I might be able to come back...
Listen... on my end...

532
00:32:10,512 --> 00:32:11,221
Listen... on my end...

533
00:32:11,221 --> 00:32:12,181
Listen... on my end...
(Gigi) But yesterday and today...

534
00:32:12,181 --> 00:32:12,556
(Gigi)
But yesterday and today...

535
00:32:12,681 --> 00:32:15,100
Quite a few transport planes have been leaving, haven't they?

536
00:32:15,225 --> 00:32:16,393
Back and forth.

537
00:32:16,852 --> 00:32:18,437
Are you spying?

538
00:32:18,562 --> 00:32:19,647
(Gigi)
For whom?

539
00:32:20,105 --> 00:32:21,482
(Kenneth)
For Hathaway, right?

540
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:26,570
(Gigi)
If I'm here,
I can see the transport planes leaving the base.

541
00:32:26,695 --> 00:32:28,739
You know that, Colonel.

542
00:32:28,864 --> 00:32:29,948
(Kenneth)
All right.

543
00:32:30,491 --> 00:32:34,328
I thought the reason the Adelaide support operation
has gone well so far...

544
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:36,413
was because you were here...

545
00:32:36,538 --> 00:32:37,289
(Gigi)
I'm glad you think so.

546
00:32:37,289 --> 00:32:39,041
(Gigi)
I'm glad you think so.
(Kenneth) What time does C38 depart tomorrow?

547
00:32:39,166 --> 00:32:40,959
(Gigi)
But even if I come see you now...

548
00:32:41,085 --> 00:32:42,378
you won't see me?

549
00:32:43,045 --> 00:32:45,714
Not tonight. Tomorrow I can come get you.

550
00:32:45,839 --> 00:32:47,216
(Gigi)
Boring.

551
00:32:47,966 --> 00:32:49,134
How boring...

552
00:32:49,802 --> 00:32:51,136
But Gigi

553
00:32:52,012 --> 00:32:54,431
That's life.

554
00:32:58,143 --> 00:32:59,978
(Hathaway)
How did it come to this?

555
00:33:00,104 --> 00:33:01,647
Colonel Kimberley Heyman

556
00:33:01,772 --> 00:33:04,983
(Kimberley) No comment.
Mafty Navue Erin

557
00:33:05,109 --> 00:33:07,986
(Raymond) We don't have truth serum either.

558
00:33:08,112 --> 00:33:09,697
Shall we torture them?

559
00:33:10,197 --> 00:33:11,615
(Hathaway) If I let that happen,

560
00:33:11,740 --> 00:33:13,742
I'd have the Oenpelli troops do it.

561
00:33:13,867 --> 00:33:14,743
(the three) Ugh...

562
00:33:14,868 --> 00:33:16,245
(Gawman) They're waiting below.

563
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:20,416
(Major) You're handing us over to them?!

564
00:33:20,541 --> 00:33:22,459
(Hathaway)
The people you detained here...

565
00:33:22,584 --> 00:33:26,422
If they knew how you dealt with them,
they'd certainly retaliate.

566
00:33:26,547 --> 00:33:28,674
(Major) Please, not that.

567
00:33:28,799 --> 00:33:30,259
(Kimberley) They're the ones...

568
00:33:31,343 --> 00:33:33,846
who cut our pilots to pieces.

569
00:33:33,971 --> 00:33:36,890
This was meant as a warning to them!

570
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:41,562
(Hala)
Lame. This is a kids' fight.

571
00:33:41,687 --> 00:33:42,646
(Kimberley, Major) Ugh...

572
00:33:44,273 --> 00:33:45,899
(Gawman) What do we do with them?

573
00:33:46,483 --> 00:33:49,862
(Hathaway) They'll slow us down,
but we can use them for prisoner exchange.

574
00:33:50,404 --> 00:33:52,531
(Gawman) Still hung up on that?

575
00:33:52,656 --> 00:33:54,742
(Hathaway)
Until that kind of thing happened...

576
00:33:54,867 --> 00:33:57,870
I couldn't even imagine it.
That's what frustrates me.

577
00:33:58,203 --> 00:34:00,330
(Gawman) Aren't you too naive?

578
00:34:02,374 --> 00:34:04,209
(Hathaway) Maybe so...

579
00:34:09,131 --> 00:34:11,425
(Gawman)
Fabio! Fabio Rivera!

580
00:34:11,842 --> 00:34:12,718
He's Mafty.

581
00:34:12,843 --> 00:34:14,136
(Oenpelli soldier) Mafty...

582
00:34:14,261 --> 00:34:15,387
(Fabio) Which one?

583
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:22,770
(Hathaway) So it's you?
The man who was posing as Mafty.

584
00:34:24,188 --> 00:34:25,481
(Fabio) Heh... Geez.

585
00:34:26,273 --> 00:34:28,150
If this isn't a joke,

586
00:34:28,275 --> 00:34:31,069
I was using some rookie's name
without knowing it.

587
00:34:31,195 --> 00:34:33,489
Seems I've dragged my own name down.

588
00:34:33,614 --> 00:34:34,698
What?!

589
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:37,910
(Oenpelli soldiers' laughter)
(Hathaway) That's because you lack imagination.

590
00:34:37,910 --> 00:34:38,619
(Hathaway) That's because you lack imagination.

591
00:34:38,744 --> 00:34:39,995
(Fabio) What did you say?

592
00:34:40,120 --> 00:34:42,581
(Hathaway) But the same goes for me.

593
00:34:43,373 --> 00:34:45,375
If there was someone impersonating Mafty,

594
00:34:45,501 --> 00:34:48,337
I thought it would be someone intelligent.

595
00:34:48,879 --> 00:34:51,173
If possible,
I'd like to meet that leader.

596
00:34:51,298 --> 00:34:52,424
Did he die?

597
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:54,343
(Fabio) What makes you say that?

598
00:34:54,468 --> 00:34:56,261
(Hathaway) A person like that...

599
00:34:56,386 --> 00:34:59,681
would fight a mobile suit with just a pistol.

600
00:34:59,807 --> 00:35:01,809
It wouldn't be surprising if he died on this battlefield.

601
00:35:01,934 --> 00:35:03,894
(Fabio) I, Fabio Rivera—

602
00:35:04,019 --> 00:35:06,980
gave the order to set up
a resistance line in this land!

603
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,649
It was only because I myself

604
00:35:08,774 --> 00:35:12,152
held the ideals of the anti-Federation movement!

605
00:35:12,277 --> 00:35:14,363
That's why I didn't run.

606
00:35:14,488 --> 00:35:17,741
We didn't even have a way
to contact Quack Salver,

607
00:35:17,866 --> 00:35:19,076
we didn't know how.

608
00:35:19,201 --> 00:35:21,578
(Federico) Fabio!
As much as that kid says,

609
00:35:21,703 --> 00:35:23,455
we haven't failed.

610
00:35:23,580 --> 00:35:27,209
Once the video reaches space,
the wind will blow our way again.

611
00:35:27,334 --> 00:35:28,252
(Hathaway) What do you mean?!

612
00:35:28,377 --> 00:35:32,256
(Fabio) With footage of the massacre
Kimberley carried out,

613
00:35:32,381 --> 00:35:34,091
our comrades are heading into space.

614
00:35:34,216 --> 00:35:35,717
(Gawman) They'll never make it.

615
00:35:35,843 --> 00:35:39,555
(Chang) Not every one of us
is an illegal squatter.

616
00:35:39,680 --> 00:35:41,640
(Hathaway)
What's on it? Is there a copy?

617
00:35:41,765 --> 00:35:43,767
(Federico) We didn't have time for that.

618
00:35:43,892 --> 00:35:47,271
(Meihou) Look,
our retreat was cut off,

619
00:35:47,396 --> 00:35:50,983
we were trampled and crushed
by mobile suits!

620
00:35:51,441 --> 00:35:52,651
(Hathaway) With mobile suits?

621
00:35:52,776 --> 00:35:56,572
(Meihou) Yeah. Kimberley toyed with us!

622
00:35:56,947 --> 00:36:00,576
(Hathaway) Even as a warning,
that's hard to believe…

623
00:36:00,701 --> 00:36:02,035
(Federico) It's no use, Meihou.

624
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,787
They only see our suffering

625
00:36:03,912 --> 00:36:06,790
from over their robots' heads.

626
00:36:06,915 --> 00:36:08,458
They're no different from Kimberley.

627
00:36:08,584 --> 00:36:09,960
(Gawman) You bastard!

628
00:36:16,550 --> 00:36:18,218
(Hathaway) We're pulling out of here.

629
00:36:19,261 --> 00:36:21,430
Take the three to Galcezon's B cabin.

630
00:36:21,555 --> 00:36:23,849
(Raymond)
Got it. What about the rest?

631
00:36:23,974 --> 00:36:26,894
(Gawman) If we leave them behind,
who knows what Fabio's people will do.

632
00:36:27,019 --> 00:36:29,771
(Hathaway) For now, we'll have to take them
and release them somewhere.

633
00:36:29,897 --> 00:36:30,689
(Member) Hey, get up.

634
00:36:30,814 --> 00:36:31,940
(Major) Ugh…

635
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:36,153
(Hathaway) We're pulling out. Let's take him in.

636
00:36:36,904 --> 00:36:38,155
(Emeralda) He's dead.

637
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:41,325
Let his comrades bury him.

638
00:36:42,701 --> 00:36:44,661
(Hathaway) That would be better…

639
00:36:54,254 --> 00:36:56,381
(Kenneth)
We let Mafty slip away.

640
00:36:56,506 --> 00:36:59,343
If we'd caught up to them at Oenpelli
yesterday,

641
00:36:59,468 --> 00:37:01,970
we could have wiped them out.

642
00:37:02,095 --> 00:37:05,807
On top of that, you have to escort cabinet ministers too.
That's a burden.

643
00:37:05,933 --> 00:37:10,020
(Kenneth) Yeah, but no matter how rotten,
they're still called cabinet ministers.

644
00:37:10,437 --> 00:37:14,650
They still order us to spread dummy intel,
so it gets in the way of real work.

645
00:37:30,832 --> 00:37:31,625
(Kenneth) Gigi.

646
00:37:32,125 --> 00:37:34,211
(Gigi) What? About the escort duty?

647
00:37:35,253 --> 00:37:38,256
Yeah.
Why did you think that?

648
00:37:38,382 --> 00:37:43,387
I never said anything about
escorting cabinet ministers just now.

649
00:37:43,512 --> 00:37:46,974
(Gigi) I don't know.
I just thought so.

650
00:37:47,474 --> 00:37:50,852
The way my heart feels lonely…

651
00:37:50,978 --> 00:37:53,563
It's the same as not being able to explain.

652
00:37:54,773 --> 00:37:58,151
Hey, tell me Hathaway Noa's
address.

653
00:37:59,319 --> 00:38:00,362
Are you going to see him?

654
00:38:00,696 --> 00:38:02,072
(Gigi) Hmph...

655
00:38:04,408 --> 00:38:05,742
Manado?

656
00:38:05,867 --> 00:38:07,828
It's way south.

657
00:38:07,953 --> 00:38:10,622
From here on, it's islands, islands, islands.

658
00:38:10,998 --> 00:38:13,333
It's all islands all the way to Australia.

659
00:38:13,750 --> 00:38:15,836
It's like a space colony.

660
00:38:15,961 --> 00:38:17,629
(Gigi) That's right.

661
00:38:17,754 --> 00:38:19,631
The sealed environment of a colony

662
00:38:19,756 --> 00:38:22,676
may have narrowed human reason, but

663
00:38:22,801 --> 00:38:26,555
I felt it's the same even on Earth.

664
00:38:27,055 --> 00:38:31,018
To me, gravity seems really oppressive.

665
00:38:31,143 --> 00:38:34,521
So, you know, going out into space
was inevitable.

666
00:38:34,646 --> 00:38:37,774
I think it's a good thing
that humans thought of that.

667
00:38:37,899 --> 00:38:41,445
Yeah. With a little more training...

668
00:38:41,570 --> 00:38:44,865
all humans might be able
to become Newtypes.

669
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:47,617
(Gigi) You're a religious man, Colonel.

670
00:38:47,743 --> 00:38:49,077
Hardly.

671
00:38:49,536 --> 00:38:52,414
I'm talking about a quality
humans are born with.

672
00:38:52,539 --> 00:38:56,418
But why would a colonel like you
get so violent?

673
00:38:57,794 --> 00:38:58,962
Violent?

674
00:38:59,087 --> 00:39:02,591
(Gigi)
Or, to put it another way, explosiveness?

675
00:39:02,883 --> 00:39:04,468
(Kenneth) You're kind.

676
00:39:04,968 --> 00:39:06,762
It's frustration, right?

677
00:39:06,887 --> 00:39:09,723
Having a body, having emotions...

678
00:39:09,848 --> 00:39:12,225
a dull human who can't reach enlightenment...

679
00:39:12,726 --> 00:39:16,021
Because I'm an Oldtype,
that's why I get irritated.

680
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:17,606
Mafty too?

681
00:39:17,731 --> 00:39:19,149
Probably...

682
00:39:20,609 --> 00:39:21,860
Yeah.

683
00:39:34,331 --> 00:39:36,166
(Bureaucrat A) The military has it tough, too.

684
00:39:36,291 --> 00:39:40,212
Seems they're putting on a show,
flying plane after plane
through this sky.

685
00:39:40,629 --> 00:39:41,421
(Bureaucrat C) To Hong Kong?

686
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:45,175
(Bureaucrat D) Picking up the minister's family
and escorting them straight to Adelaide.

687
00:39:45,550 --> 00:39:47,344
(Bureaucrat C) That's rough...

688
00:39:47,469 --> 00:39:48,845
(Bureaucrat D) Heh. What about you?

689
00:39:48,970 --> 00:39:53,141
(Bureaucrat C) I'm in the second half of the conference,
so I'll head to Adelaide in a week.

690
00:39:54,684 --> 00:39:56,311
(Kimberley soldier) Nn...

691
00:39:58,396 --> 00:40:01,149
We've been set free, huh...

692
00:40:15,372 --> 00:40:16,832
(Hathaway)
See you at the wall! Gawman.

693
00:40:17,332 --> 00:40:18,458
Take the Sea Rack!

694
00:40:18,834 --> 00:40:19,960
Mafty too!

695
00:40:28,051 --> 00:40:29,386
(Gigi) More than Davao?

696
00:40:29,845 --> 00:40:32,097
(Wave) Especially the places Lady Gigi
is about to visit...

697
00:40:32,222 --> 00:40:34,975
Using a limousine is
a privileged act.

698
00:40:34,975 --> 00:40:35,475
Using a limousine is
a privileged act.
(civilian)
Please stop it!

699
00:40:35,475 --> 00:40:35,725
(civilian)
Please stop it!

700
00:40:35,725 --> 00:40:36,852
(civilian)
Please stop it!
You'd better tip the driver
in advance.

701
00:40:36,852 --> 00:40:38,478
You'd better tip the driver
in advance.

702
00:40:38,478 --> 00:40:38,895
You'd better tip the driver
in advance.
(Man Hunter)
Don't move!

703
00:40:38,895 --> 00:40:39,271
(Man Hunter)
Don't move!

704
00:40:39,271 --> 00:40:39,771
(Man Hunter)
Don't move!
(Gigi) Even if a soldier like you asks?

705
00:40:39,771 --> 00:40:41,565
(Gigi) Even if a soldier like you asks?

706
00:40:42,315 --> 00:40:44,860
Yes, the Federation government's crackdown

707
00:40:44,985 --> 00:40:47,195
is making ordinary people violent
in some places.

708
00:40:47,737 --> 00:40:49,781
Retaliation using Man Hunters and the like

709
00:40:49,906 --> 00:40:51,992
will come to the privileged class.

710
00:40:57,539 --> 00:41:00,333
(Minister) When I got off the ship,
I thought I'd stepped into the water.

711
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:02,961
(Friend) This slimy stuff
is Earth.

712
00:41:03,962 --> 00:41:05,463
(Wave) Sorry to keep you waiting!

713
00:41:07,132 --> 00:41:09,509
Ms. Mace Flower,
this way, please.

714
00:41:37,495 --> 00:41:39,915
(Driver) Even so,
compared to the old century's prosperity,

715
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,875
it's only a tenth.

716
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:45,420
But the Federation government's recent
push to return to Earth

717
00:41:45,545 --> 00:41:46,922
is remarkable.

718
00:41:58,975 --> 00:42:00,268
(Driver)
The Universal Century is

719
00:42:00,393 --> 00:42:01,978
already a century old.

720
00:42:02,103 --> 00:42:04,314
They say Earth's pollution has eased, so

721
00:42:04,439 --> 00:42:06,691
even in the city and in high-class residential areas like this,

722
00:42:06,816 --> 00:42:09,152
government officials... ah...

723
00:42:10,570 --> 00:42:15,075
(Gigi) It's fine. I'm not
from that class.

724
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:18,662
I'm just someone with the pathetic job
of being a mistress.

725
00:42:18,787 --> 00:42:21,164
(Driver) Oh... Hahaha...

726
00:42:21,289 --> 00:42:24,167
Hearing you say that
makes me feel better.

727
00:42:34,010 --> 00:42:35,428
(Guard) Only residents are allowed in.

728
00:42:36,805 --> 00:42:40,058
(Gigi) Gigi Andalusia...
Surely you've heard of me?

729
00:42:42,102 --> 00:42:43,061
(Guard) Oh!

730
00:42:43,186 --> 00:42:45,814
You arrived later than expected.
We were worried.

731
00:42:46,356 --> 00:42:48,441
I came down on the Haunzen Flight.

732
00:42:48,566 --> 00:42:49,985
(gate opens)

733
00:42:55,115 --> 00:42:57,075
(Caretaker) Your room is on the top floor.

734
00:42:57,200 --> 00:43:00,287
The view
is simply wonderful.

735
00:43:00,412 --> 00:43:01,788
(Gigi) I should hope so.

736
00:43:01,913 --> 00:43:03,540
If I'm disappointed,

737
00:43:03,665 --> 00:43:06,543
there'd be no point in coming
to a place like this.

738
00:43:06,668 --> 00:43:07,836
(Caretaker) Quite right...

739
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:12,173
(Caretaker) I've had the minimum preparations done,
such as making the bed.

740
00:43:12,299 --> 00:43:14,384
If you need new things,

741
00:43:14,509 --> 00:43:16,970
I'll call a contractor right away.

742
00:43:27,689 --> 00:43:28,606
(Gigi) The elevator?

743
00:43:28,732 --> 00:43:29,858
(Caretaker) Yes!

744
00:43:30,567 --> 00:43:32,110
This way!

745
00:43:46,416 --> 00:43:47,876
(Caretaker) Here we go.

746
00:43:50,253 --> 00:43:53,882
You're welcome to purchase the furniture as is.

747
00:43:54,007 --> 00:43:55,759
We also have catalogs available.

748
00:43:56,843 --> 00:43:57,802
(Gigi) I see.

749
00:43:59,929 --> 00:44:03,475
♪～

750
00:44:03,600 --> 00:44:07,520
♪ I had a sudden feeling.

751
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:10,815
♪ Before the magic fades

752
00:44:11,399 --> 00:44:15,320
♪ I want to blend together and know

753
00:44:15,445 --> 00:44:18,740
♪ Unmixed expectations

754
00:44:18,865 --> 00:44:22,494
♪ With a feigned attitude

755
00:44:22,619 --> 00:44:26,039
♪ With my real feelings about to fade

756
00:44:26,164 --> 00:44:28,958
♪ I can't keep up the act anymore

757
00:44:30,377 --> 00:44:34,589
♪ In front of you, I distort

758
00:44:34,714 --> 00:44:36,841
♪ Steal me to go

759
00:44:36,966 --> 00:44:38,426
♪ The boiling STROKE

760
00:44:38,551 --> 00:44:42,972
♪ Even in a world that bypassed the right answer

761
00:44:43,098 --> 00:44:44,766
♪ Divert me so

762
00:44:44,891 --> 00:44:46,851
♪ The PAST I entrusted

763
00:44:46,976 --> 00:44:50,647
♪ Even a wish clouded by afterimages is fine

764
00:44:50,772 --> 00:44:54,776
♪ Cuz I define you
   lying with your breath

765
00:44:54,901 --> 00:44:58,905
♪ A blue about to overflow and burst

766
00:44:59,030 --> 00:45:02,409
♪ I want to touch you more selfishly and it hurts

767
00:45:02,951 --> 00:45:06,746
♪ If we sink while embracing

768
00:45:06,871 --> 00:45:08,748
♪ Steal me to go

769
00:45:08,873 --> 00:45:10,708
♪ The boiling STROKE

770
00:45:10,834 --> 00:45:14,796
♪ Even in a world that bypassed the right answer

771
00:45:14,921 --> 00:45:16,798
♪ Divert me so

772
00:45:16,923 --> 00:45:18,842
♪ The PAST I entrusted

773
00:45:18,967 --> 00:45:22,762
♪ Even a wish clouded by afterimages is fine

774
00:45:22,887 --> 00:45:27,100
♪ Cuz I define you
   lying with your breath

775
00:45:27,225 --> 00:45:31,104
♪ A blue about to overflow and burst

776
00:45:33,106 --> 00:45:34,482
(Gigi) Hah!

777
00:45:47,245 --> 00:45:48,746
Hathaway, huh...

778
00:45:51,666 --> 00:45:53,793
(sound of entering the bath)

779
00:45:58,756 --> 00:46:00,008
(Gigi) Hathaway Noa

780
00:46:01,092 --> 00:46:03,261
Hathaway Noa

781
00:46:04,137 --> 00:46:06,723
Hathaway Noa

782
00:46:09,309 --> 00:46:10,852
Hathaway, huh...

783
00:46:12,937 --> 00:46:15,857
(Gigi, voiceover)
I can't face Grandfather...

784
00:46:28,661 --> 00:46:30,705
(Hathaway) Did you send Kelia
to Darwin?

785
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:33,458
(Iram) Yeah.
The captain complained, but

786
00:46:33,833 --> 00:46:36,377
there are also preparations over there
to receive them,

787
00:46:36,503 --> 00:46:37,670
so I sent her with Julia.

788
00:46:37,795 --> 00:46:38,755
Julia?

789
00:46:39,589 --> 00:46:41,633
Those two, who don't get along?

790
00:46:46,471 --> 00:46:48,097
(Amuro) After you've smelled the stench of death,

791
00:46:48,223 --> 00:46:50,600
you worry about Kelia?

792
00:46:50,725 --> 00:46:52,852
(Hathaway)
I'm supposed to have a great cause—

793
00:46:52,977 --> 00:46:55,688
to give the world
the impact of social reform.

794
00:46:56,481 --> 00:46:59,150
Gigi was meant for that...

795
00:46:59,275 --> 00:47:01,528
(Quess)
No one's going to believe that!

796
00:47:07,575 --> 00:47:08,493
(Hathaway) Yeah...

797
00:47:11,162 --> 00:47:14,499
Somehow, I have to break away

798
00:47:14,624 --> 00:47:16,000
from this body and these emotional desires,

799
00:47:16,376 --> 00:47:18,336
or I won't be saved...

800
00:47:22,215 --> 00:47:24,884
(Iram)
That'll be the last of that.

801
00:47:25,009 --> 00:47:25,843
(Hathaway) Huh?

802
00:47:25,969 --> 00:47:28,555
(Iram) Kelia
procured it for you, didn't she?

803
00:47:31,432 --> 00:47:32,600
I see.

804
00:47:34,269 --> 00:47:36,854
You regret it now, don't you?

805
00:47:37,397 --> 00:47:39,816
(Hathaway)
Stop it, I give, I give!

806
00:47:39,941 --> 00:47:41,693
(both laugh)

807
00:47:44,362 --> 00:47:45,196
(Hathaway) Heh.

808
00:47:46,281 --> 00:47:48,783
(Iram)
Since then, Davao and Hong Kong

809
00:47:48,908 --> 00:47:50,868
radio exchanges with Guangzhou

810
00:47:50,994 --> 00:47:53,162
have become more and more contrived.

811
00:47:53,580 --> 00:47:56,124
But there are also a lot of southbound transport planes.

812
00:47:56,749 --> 00:48:00,378
We still can't rule out
that both are diversions.

813
00:48:00,503 --> 00:48:02,589
(Hathaway)
But there isn't that much leeway

814
00:48:02,714 --> 00:48:04,507
even for the Kirke unit.

815
00:48:04,841 --> 00:48:06,426
(Iram) I suppose so, but—

816
00:48:06,551 --> 00:48:09,262
Since Kenneth Sleg arrived,
Davao's movements have been

817
00:48:09,387 --> 00:48:11,180
remarkably active.

818
00:48:11,598 --> 00:48:12,807
He's certainly a capable operator.

819
00:48:12,932 --> 00:48:14,726
Hm... is that so?

820
00:48:15,393 --> 00:48:17,979
At Bynoe, at least,
there'll be some resupply, right?

821
00:48:18,104 --> 00:48:20,189
(Iram) Yeah, that's the plan.

822
00:48:20,315 --> 00:48:23,901
They'll take care of the
Heso Point and Gora matter.

823
00:48:24,360 --> 00:48:25,903
(Iram) Kelia, she...
(Hathaway) Oof!

824
00:48:27,030 --> 00:48:27,822
(Hathaway) Nngh!

825
00:48:40,460 --> 00:48:43,504
(Kenneth) Hm... heh heh.

826
00:48:44,005 --> 00:48:45,715
(Mace) Heheheh...

827
00:49:23,753 --> 00:49:25,129
(Clerk) I'll put you through.

828
00:49:25,254 --> 00:49:26,214
(phone hold music)

829
00:49:28,174 --> 00:49:29,884
(hold music)

830
00:49:31,761 --> 00:49:34,305
(Gigi) Is Hathaway Noa in?

831
00:49:35,306 --> 00:49:37,016
(a man resembling Amada) No, he's out.

832
00:49:37,141 --> 00:49:39,852
He's out on field training.
He isn't here.

833
00:49:42,772 --> 00:49:45,692
Are you Professor Amada Mansan?

834
00:49:45,817 --> 00:49:46,901
(a man resembling Amada) Who may I ask is calling?

835
00:49:47,026 --> 00:49:49,320
(Gigi)
My name is Gigi Andalucia.

836
00:49:49,946 --> 00:49:53,074
(a man resembling Amada) I've heard the name.
Where are you calling from?

837
00:49:53,199 --> 00:49:54,701
(Gigi) Hong Kong.

838
00:49:54,826 --> 00:49:57,954
Actually, I'd love to visit you there, but...

839
00:49:58,287 --> 00:50:00,206
Could you pass a message to Hathaway?

840
00:50:00,331 --> 00:50:01,207
(a man resembling Amada) Certainly.

841
00:50:05,002 --> 00:50:06,045
Tell him our next date—

842
00:50:06,170 --> 00:50:08,464
let's make it Adelaide.

843
00:50:08,589 --> 00:50:10,425
(a man resembling Amada)
A date in Adelaide?

844
00:50:10,550 --> 00:50:12,427
That's rather out of the blue.

845
00:50:12,802 --> 00:50:14,804
(Gigi) We decided that yesterday.

846
00:50:14,929 --> 00:50:18,141
We couldn't decide on our next meeting in Davao...

847
00:50:18,516 --> 00:50:21,769
(a man resembling Amada) His work takes him
to places with no phones, so...

848
00:50:21,894 --> 00:50:25,523
Unless I hear from him,
there's nothing I can do.

849
00:50:25,648 --> 00:50:28,943
(Gigi) I don't know yet
what I'll do either.

850
00:50:29,318 --> 00:50:32,321
I might go to Uncle Kenneth's place...

851
00:50:32,447 --> 00:50:33,990
(a man resembling Amada) Uncle Kenneth?

852
00:50:34,115 --> 00:50:36,284
Ah... You're a busy one, aren't you?

853
00:50:36,409 --> 00:50:39,746
That's right.
I have a lot of fans, don't I?

854
00:50:39,871 --> 00:50:42,582
But I'm glad
this call got through...

855
00:50:43,166 --> 00:50:44,876
Can I call you again?

856
00:50:45,001 --> 00:50:46,961
(a man resembling Amada) I don't mind that, but...

857
00:51:02,268 --> 00:51:03,895
(Gigi, voiceover) It's all right, isn't it...

858
00:51:10,735 --> 00:51:13,780
(Yeoksan) Thank you for your cooperation
in yesterday's operation.

859
00:51:13,905 --> 00:51:16,741
No, not at all.
While we'll be away for a while,

860
00:51:16,866 --> 00:51:19,535
we wanted things kept quiet.

861
00:51:19,660 --> 00:51:20,453
(Hugest) Indeed.

862
00:51:22,872 --> 00:51:23,664
(Kenneth) Mm.

863
00:51:23,790 --> 00:51:26,292
(Lagoid)
Yes, sir! Here!

864
00:51:26,417 --> 00:51:29,879
(Yeoksan) For someone stuck
on Earth, he's quite capable.

865
00:51:31,631 --> 00:51:34,801
I thought you'd also
be pulled into the military.

866
00:51:35,092 --> 00:51:36,969
You're Bright Noa's son, aren't you?

867
00:51:38,971 --> 00:51:40,681
He seems to have returned to Menado.

868
00:51:41,390 --> 00:51:43,267
Did you track him?

869
00:51:43,392 --> 00:51:45,853
Even if the passengers of that craft
are cabinet ministers' families,

870
00:51:45,978 --> 00:51:47,980
we still track them.

871
00:51:48,648 --> 00:51:51,150
Man Hunter is a tough job.

872
00:51:51,692 --> 00:51:52,985
I see...

873
00:51:54,195 --> 00:51:55,446
How dull...

874
00:51:55,571 --> 00:51:58,991
(Yeoksan)
Heh... Right, that girl Gigi.

875
00:51:59,116 --> 00:52:01,661
You were right to stay away from her.

876
00:52:01,786 --> 00:52:05,832
If you get involved with Cardeas,
you'll have no future as an officer.

877
00:52:06,123 --> 00:52:07,041
(Kenneth) I'll take that to heart.

878
00:52:09,168 --> 00:52:10,419
(Yeoksan) I see.

879
00:52:14,465 --> 00:52:17,176
(Jose) This woman Mace is
on the Haunzen as
a CA.

880
00:52:17,552 --> 00:52:19,595
Her identity is guaranteed, I hear.

881
00:52:19,720 --> 00:52:20,930
(Silva) What's the source?

882
00:52:21,347 --> 00:52:23,850
(Jose) A reliable source:
Lieutenant Ray Lagoid.

883
00:52:23,975 --> 00:52:25,893
(laughter)
(Okamura) What's that?

884
00:52:26,018 --> 00:52:27,103
(Sojin) Rejected.

885
00:52:27,228 --> 00:52:29,897
She's an illegal resident
living in Hong Kong,

886
00:52:30,022 --> 00:52:31,482
sent to get information
from Kenneth.

887
00:52:31,607 --> 00:52:34,360
A spy dispatched by Mafty.

888
00:52:34,485 --> 00:52:35,695
(Eikka) That's just great.
(laughter)

889
00:52:35,695 --> 00:52:35,820
(laughter)

890
00:52:35,820 --> 00:52:37,113
(laughter)
(Sojin) It's funny, right?

891
00:52:37,113 --> 00:52:38,364
(laughter)

892
00:52:38,489 --> 00:52:40,741
(announcer) This time,
the Kirke unit and the police organization

893
00:52:40,867 --> 00:52:44,203
jointly commanded
a sweep operation against subversive elements.

894
00:52:44,328 --> 00:52:48,082
It appears there were over 500 arrests
and over 100 deaths.

895
00:52:48,207 --> 00:52:50,501
The military and Man Hunter...

896
00:52:50,626 --> 00:52:52,795
What's going on, Kenneth?

897
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:04,891
(female newscaster)
Pollution remediation in the Southern Hemisphere...

898
00:53:05,016 --> 00:53:06,893
(weather forecaster)
The westerlies, which have been meandering greatly...

899
00:53:07,018 --> 00:53:07,894
(both laugh)

900
00:53:09,770 --> 00:53:10,938
(narrator)
Space colonies...

901
00:53:11,063 --> 00:53:13,691
(Gigi) Even if I stay here,
I can't hear the truth.

902
00:53:13,816 --> 00:53:16,527
(female newscaster)
That's all for today.
Have a good day tomorrow.

903
00:53:16,652 --> 00:53:17,695
Good night.

904
00:53:19,989 --> 00:53:23,075
(alarm)

905
00:53:23,534 --> 00:53:25,202
(Gigi) Mm! Mm!

906
00:53:34,795 --> 00:53:36,130
I'm sorry.

907
00:53:36,255 --> 00:53:39,091
I still want to live a little longer.

908
00:53:55,316 --> 00:53:58,027
This is my fate.

909
00:54:01,405 --> 00:54:03,366
(Gigi, voiceover) I feel sorry for the Count, too.

910
00:54:08,329 --> 00:54:10,790
Adieu, my patron.

911
00:54:12,500 --> 00:54:13,793
I...

912
00:54:14,085 --> 00:54:16,295
may be going to my death.

913
00:54:26,931 --> 00:54:27,765
(Hathaway) From the professor?

914
00:54:28,265 --> 00:54:31,018
(Wedge) Yeah.
If the decryption is correct.

915
00:54:31,143 --> 00:54:33,604
Apparently, no change—
it's still Adelaide.

916
00:54:34,480 --> 00:54:35,398
(Hathaway) Gigi?

917
00:54:35,856 --> 00:54:38,317
I see. So it came from her...

918
00:54:41,570 --> 00:54:43,239
(Wedge) Is she all right?

919
00:54:43,614 --> 00:54:46,575
(Hathaway) That girl, in the sense that
her mood changes constantly...

920
00:54:46,701 --> 00:54:48,327
she seems special.

921
00:54:48,452 --> 00:54:49,453
(Wedge) Is that so?

922
00:54:52,999 --> 00:54:55,584
You know her? Gigi?

923
00:54:56,544 --> 00:54:59,839
Girls like Gigi aren't rare.

924
00:55:03,968 --> 00:55:06,846
(Hathaway)
There's one interesting possibility.

925
00:55:07,388 --> 00:55:08,180
(Wedge) Oh?

926
00:55:09,807 --> 00:55:11,183
Fabio Rivera and his people

927
00:55:11,308 --> 00:55:13,728
may be moving into
Bynoe Harbour.

928
00:55:13,853 --> 00:55:16,605
How do they see
Kirke's movements?

929
00:55:16,981 --> 00:55:21,068
(Hathaway) They'll see it as a diversion
to keep us pinned on that continent.

930
00:55:21,193 --> 00:55:24,447
In that sense,
Fabio and his people are too clever.

931
00:55:24,572 --> 00:55:26,991
(Iram) Since right after Hathaway
landed in Davao,

932
00:55:27,116 --> 00:55:30,494
communications between Davao and Hong Kong
have been on the rise.

933
00:55:30,619 --> 00:55:33,998
There are reports the Federation cabinet meeting
has been moved to Kwangchow.

934
00:55:34,123 --> 00:55:35,875
There's reason to believe that.

935
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:39,545
Hundley Yeoksan of the Criminal Police Organization
is sharp, too.

936
00:55:39,670 --> 00:55:43,132
It was him and Kenneth
who set the Man Hunter in motion, right?

937
00:55:43,257 --> 00:55:45,509
So that means today or tomorrow

938
00:55:45,634 --> 00:55:48,012
all cabinet ministers
will move to Adelaide.

939
00:55:48,471 --> 00:55:49,346
Right.

940
00:55:49,472 --> 00:55:51,932
Around Hong Kong,
how many were there?

941
00:55:52,058 --> 00:55:54,268
(Wedge)
About twelve, I'd say.

942
00:55:54,393 --> 00:55:58,606
There are flights from South America, too,
so transport capacity has been built up.

943
00:55:58,939 --> 00:56:02,443
But the enemy's insistence
on Adelaide for the cabinet meeting—

944
00:56:02,568 --> 00:56:03,736
What's their scheme?

945
00:56:04,153 --> 00:56:07,198
Using the Kirke unit
and the Criminal Police Organization,

946
00:56:07,323 --> 00:56:10,451
they intend to crush us completely.

947
00:56:10,576 --> 00:56:12,369
The Federation government believes

948
00:56:12,495 --> 00:56:14,622
it's in command,
so

949
00:56:14,747 --> 00:56:16,248
that's why it's Adelaide.

950
00:56:16,832 --> 00:56:19,168
That's your gut feeling from meeting
the cabinet ministers?

951
00:56:19,293 --> 00:56:20,127
(Hathaway) Yeah.

952
00:56:20,252 --> 00:56:21,420
(Wedge) I don't get it...

953
00:56:21,837 --> 00:56:24,590
Somehow your thinking
feels... insular.

954
00:56:24,715 --> 00:56:27,510
(Iram)
That's why it's 'overthrow the Federation government,' right!

955
00:56:27,635 --> 00:56:28,427
Hathaway!

956
00:56:28,552 --> 00:56:29,386
(Hathaway) Yeah.

957
00:56:35,351 --> 00:56:36,560
Is Gigi really that...

958
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:37,603
Is Gigi really that...
(Wedge) I don't know her.

959
00:56:38,312 --> 00:56:39,897
That's how Mihessia and the others rate her.

960
00:56:40,356 --> 00:56:44,026
Mihessia's the type who feels too much.
She's not much use as a reference.

961
00:56:44,151 --> 00:56:45,402
(Wedge) Is that so?

962
00:56:46,987 --> 00:56:48,030
(Hathaway) It's fine.

963
00:56:53,452 --> 00:56:57,123
(Iram) The crew assignments for each Base Jabber
are as listed.

964
00:56:57,248 --> 00:56:58,874
After resupplying at Bynoe,

965
00:56:58,999 --> 00:57:01,919
we split into four teams
and head for Navel Point.

966
00:57:02,336 --> 00:57:05,506
(Emeralda) Aren't there relief personnel for us
even at the continent's navel?

967
00:57:05,631 --> 00:57:06,632
(Hathaway)
Quack Salver is

968
00:57:06,757 --> 00:57:09,009
doing what they can, but...

969
00:57:09,552 --> 00:57:10,594
It's wishful thinking.

970
00:57:11,137 --> 00:57:13,639
But if the Base Jabbers are reinforced,

971
00:57:13,764 --> 00:57:15,724
they might be bringing

972
00:57:15,850 --> 00:57:17,476
some new faces we don't know.

973
00:57:17,601 --> 00:57:19,145
(Rod) That would be nice.

974
00:57:19,270 --> 00:57:20,980
You'd pray to God for that?

975
00:57:21,856 --> 00:57:24,108
What about Gawman and the others at Sealuck?

976
00:57:24,233 --> 00:57:24,733
(Golf) They're passing through.

977
00:57:24,733 --> 00:57:25,609
(Golf) They're passing through.
(Hathaway) We can't link up with them until the Wall,

978
00:57:25,609 --> 00:57:26,235
(Hathaway) We can't link up with them until the Wall,

979
00:57:26,652 --> 00:57:28,362
but there seems to be mobile suit reinforcements.

980
00:57:28,487 --> 00:57:29,280
(Golf) Huh...

981
00:57:29,405 --> 00:57:31,407
(Raymond) Mafty can't be taken lightly either, you know.

982
00:57:31,866 --> 00:57:32,658
(Raymond) Tch...
(Emeralda) Too close...

983
00:57:33,325 --> 00:57:35,119
(Raymond)
What? Don't get so embarrassed.

984
00:57:35,244 --> 00:57:35,578
(Iram)
Anyway, once we reach the Wall,

985
00:57:35,578 --> 00:57:36,662
(Iram)
Anyway, once we reach the Wall,
(Emeralda)
Don't be stupid.

986
00:57:36,662 --> 00:57:37,454
(Iram)
Anyway, once we reach the Wall,

987
00:57:37,580 --> 00:57:39,999
there'll be support for the Adelaide attack.

988
00:57:40,124 --> 00:57:42,501
After that, until the Wall,
without getting caught in Kirke's net,

989
00:57:42,626 --> 00:57:44,044
we just have to keep moving.

990
00:57:44,170 --> 00:57:45,462
(Hendrix) The problem is,

991
00:57:45,588 --> 00:57:47,965
from Bynoe Harbour to Navel Point

992
00:57:48,090 --> 00:57:50,384
we'll be operating in three-man cells.

993
00:57:50,843 --> 00:57:53,304
We can't afford to be wiped out.

994
00:57:53,804 --> 00:57:55,222
(Hala) Ah...
(Golf) Whoo...

995
00:57:55,806 --> 00:57:58,767
(Hathaway) Fortunately, the enemy is
hinting at Kwangchow,

996
00:57:59,185 --> 00:58:01,270
so they're not making any obvious move south.

997
00:58:01,395 --> 00:58:03,022
Even so...

998
00:58:03,147 --> 00:58:05,816
(Ridorick)
Well, if the timing's right,

999
00:58:05,941 --> 00:58:08,611
we can hit Kirke's vanguard.

1000
00:58:08,736 --> 00:58:11,363
(Hendrix) Since when did Rid become
an optimist?

1001
00:58:11,488 --> 00:58:12,281
(Rod) What's in it for us?

1002
00:58:12,740 --> 00:58:13,657
(Iram) Nothing.

1003
00:58:13,782 --> 00:58:16,076
The self-satisfaction
of having done what we could.

1004
00:58:16,202 --> 00:58:17,912
Just self-satisfaction.

1005
00:58:18,996 --> 00:58:22,666
I'm sorry, but as we are now,
we have no choice but to move forward.

1006
00:58:24,251 --> 00:58:25,252
Bear with me.

1007
00:58:35,095 --> 00:58:35,888
(Lane's Mechanic A) Hey, hey.

1008
00:58:36,597 --> 00:58:38,641
What's wrong with the colonel's
nerves?!

1009
00:58:40,768 --> 00:58:43,854
She's different from the woman
the colonel's been with lately, right?

1010
00:58:43,979 --> 00:58:45,814
(Lane's Mechanic C)
She's different! Totally different!

1011
00:58:50,444 --> 00:58:51,278
(Lane) Ah!

1012
00:58:52,321 --> 00:58:54,198
(Lane's Mechanic C)
Right in front of subordinates about to deploy,

1013
00:58:54,323 --> 00:58:57,284
What's the colonel doing?

1014
00:58:58,118 --> 00:59:01,121
(Lane, voiceover)
Gigi... So that was her name...

1015
00:59:01,997 --> 00:59:04,541
(Lane's Mechanic D)
That's the colonel's good-luck charm, right? That one!

1016
00:59:04,667 --> 00:59:05,793
(Lane's Mechanic B)
She came back?

1017
00:59:05,918 --> 00:59:06,710
(Lane's Mechanic D) Looks like it.

1018
00:59:08,170 --> 00:59:09,380
(Lane, voiceover) A good-luck charm...?

1019
00:59:13,175 --> 00:59:15,970
Huh!? ... What the...?

1020
00:59:23,227 --> 00:59:24,186
(Lagoid) Move out!

1021
00:59:35,906 --> 00:59:38,993
(Lane's Mechanic B)
We'll reach the west route
by nightfall.

1022
00:59:39,868 --> 00:59:41,245
(Lane's Mechanic A)
As the colonel said,

1023
00:59:41,370 --> 00:59:43,872
I hope we find
Mafty's support base.

1024
00:59:44,164 --> 00:59:44,957
Yeah.

1025
00:59:46,292 --> 00:59:47,626
(Lane, voiceover) As if you'll find it.

1026
00:59:53,757 --> 00:59:55,217
(Gigi) It's an awful place.

1027
00:59:55,634 --> 00:59:57,261
So I came back.

1028
00:59:57,386 --> 01:00:00,097
I don't care about the Count
anymore.

1029
01:00:00,848 --> 01:00:02,266
I understand.

1030
01:00:02,683 --> 01:00:04,476
I can't keep you company for a while.

1031
01:00:04,601 --> 01:00:06,562
(Gigi) I'm going to Adelaide.

1032
01:00:06,687 --> 01:00:07,479
That's right.

1033
01:00:07,604 --> 01:00:10,899
Then maybe I'll hide out
at Hathaway's place.

1034
01:00:11,025 --> 01:00:14,236
The Count won't come after me
as far as Menado, right?

1035
01:00:14,611 --> 01:00:15,988
(Kenneth) I suppose so.

1036
01:00:19,825 --> 01:00:21,410
(Kenneth) Where did you put your luggage?

1037
01:00:23,120 --> 01:00:26,165
(Gigi) I found a luggage storage place
in Hong Kong.

1038
01:00:26,290 --> 01:00:29,376
(Kenneth) I'll have it sent.
You have the claim tag, right?

1039
01:00:29,501 --> 01:00:30,878
(Gigi) I'm not sure.

1040
01:00:31,003 --> 01:00:32,671
If Hathaway gets mad at me,

1041
01:00:32,796 --> 01:00:35,257
I'll have to go back
to Hong Kong, right?

1042
01:00:35,382 --> 01:00:38,385
Then
come to me.

1043
01:00:38,510 --> 01:00:40,012
I'll work something out.

1044
01:00:40,679 --> 01:00:41,847
(Gigi) No.

1045
01:00:42,306 --> 01:00:45,601
Something scary happened
in Davao yesterday, right?

1046
01:00:45,726 --> 01:00:48,562
(Kenneth)
That was all. Nothing since.

1047
01:00:48,687 --> 01:00:51,607
The Adelaide Conference
won't last forever.

1048
01:00:55,861 --> 01:00:56,653
Hello!

1049
01:00:56,779 --> 01:00:58,113
(Duty Soldier) Uh... ah...

1050
01:00:58,739 --> 01:00:59,740
(Gigi) Hmm?

1051
01:01:00,532 --> 01:01:03,202
(Kenneth) It's about her.
Can I ask a favor?

1052
01:01:05,329 --> 01:01:07,414
(Francine) Huh? ... Yes.

1053
01:01:07,956 --> 01:01:09,583
(Kenneth) Hmm?
(Gigi) Shall I step outside?

1054
01:01:09,708 --> 01:01:11,210
(footsteps)

1055
01:01:11,627 --> 01:01:12,836
(Mace) Shall we depart?

1056
01:01:14,671 --> 01:01:17,424
Ah... Gigi Andalusia.

1057
01:01:17,549 --> 01:01:19,843
(Kenneth) Yeah.
I'll take Gigi partway too.

1058
01:01:19,968 --> 01:01:22,638
(Mace)
Colonel? Lieutenant Colonel Meinzer is—

1059
01:01:22,971 --> 01:01:23,806
(Kenneth) Hmm...?

1060
01:01:26,892 --> 01:01:28,394
Wait here a moment.

1061
01:01:28,894 --> 01:01:29,895
(Kenneth's subordinate) This way.

1062
01:01:38,946 --> 01:01:40,823
(Mace) Were you in Davao
this whole time?

1063
01:01:41,198 --> 01:01:44,284
(Gigi) No.
I just got back from Hong Kong today.

1064
01:01:44,410 --> 01:01:46,495
(Mace)
Then I got back before you.

1065
01:01:46,620 --> 01:01:48,872
From Hong Kong—
looking after the VIPs.

1066
01:01:48,997 --> 01:01:50,582
Then I got sent to Davao again.

1067
01:01:51,083 --> 01:01:53,210
I lost my leave.

1068
01:01:53,335 --> 01:01:54,837
(Gigi) When it comes to Mafty countermeasures,

1069
01:01:54,962 --> 01:01:58,090
The brass don't want to use people they don't know.

1070
01:01:58,215 --> 01:02:01,927
You seem to be well liked by everyone here.

1071
01:02:02,052 --> 01:02:03,303
(Gigi) That's what I hated.

1072
01:02:03,887 --> 01:02:07,850
(Gigi) The Colonel saved me from that...
is more accurate.

1073
01:02:07,975 --> 01:02:09,143
(Mace) Ah...

1074
01:02:09,268 --> 01:02:11,353
Men really are children, aren't they?

1075
01:02:13,605 --> 01:02:18,193
(Gigi) I wanted to see the Colonel
try his luck as a soldier.

1076
01:02:18,318 --> 01:02:19,695
So I stayed by his side.

1077
01:02:20,112 --> 01:02:21,155
Luck?

1078
01:02:22,281 --> 01:02:23,365
Huh.

1079
01:02:23,490 --> 01:02:25,951
So that's why it's a middle-aged guy?

1080
01:02:27,411 --> 01:02:28,245
Heh.

1081
01:02:29,079 --> 01:02:30,789
The Colonel, you know...

1082
01:02:31,623 --> 01:02:34,376
(whispering)

1083
01:02:34,918 --> 01:02:37,379
(Gigi) Hehehe, heh, hehehe.

1084
01:02:37,504 --> 01:02:38,338
What?!

1085
01:02:40,090 --> 01:02:40,924
(slap)

1086
01:02:51,810 --> 01:02:54,146
(Meinzer)
The security shift has been changed.

1087
01:02:54,396 --> 01:02:55,022
(Kenneth) Hmm?

1088
01:03:00,360 --> 01:03:01,153
What is it?

1089
01:03:01,278 --> 01:03:03,655
(Francine) Oh, um... um...

1090
01:03:03,989 --> 01:03:06,408
(Gigi)
Mace says she's leaving.

1091
01:03:06,867 --> 01:03:08,160
To Hong Kong?

1092
01:03:08,285 --> 01:03:09,536
(Gigi) Yes...

1093
01:03:10,871 --> 01:03:12,289
(Kenneth) You chased her off, huh?

1094
01:03:12,414 --> 01:03:13,207
(Gigi) Yeah...

1095
01:03:13,916 --> 01:03:15,459
I thought so...

1096
01:03:17,961 --> 01:03:19,338
(Gigi) Sorry!

1097
01:03:24,134 --> 01:03:25,719
But that woman...

1098
01:03:25,844 --> 01:03:27,721
Not now.

1099
01:03:27,846 --> 01:03:30,182
She'll drain your energy, Colonel.

1100
01:03:31,892 --> 01:03:33,060
I see...

1101
01:03:33,477 --> 01:03:35,854
If Gigi says so, it must be true.

1102
01:03:35,979 --> 01:03:40,234
In return, I'll stay by the Colonel's side a little longer.

1103
01:03:40,901 --> 01:03:42,611
(Kenneth) It's Australia!

1104
01:03:43,237 --> 01:03:44,363
(Gigi) Sure.

1105
01:03:45,572 --> 01:03:50,994
(English announcement)

1106
01:03:52,746 --> 01:03:54,414
(Kenneth)
Well? Think it'll go well?

1107
01:03:54,540 --> 01:03:56,833
(Gigi) The whole operation, you mean?

1108
01:03:56,959 --> 01:03:58,669
Or this transport plane...?

1109
01:03:58,794 --> 01:04:01,338
(Kenneth)
Both. Everything.

1110
01:04:01,463 --> 01:04:03,173
(Gigi)
I'm not a fortune teller.

1111
01:04:03,298 --> 01:04:04,716
(Officer) Who's that?
(Gigi) But...

1112
01:04:05,259 --> 01:04:07,010
I think it'll go well.

1113
01:04:07,511 --> 01:04:10,222
Whether you can catch anything of Mafty...

1114
01:04:10,681 --> 01:04:13,100
I think it'll slip underwater.

1115
01:04:13,559 --> 01:04:14,643
(Kenneth) Underwater?

1116
01:04:14,768 --> 01:04:16,270
(Gigi) Something like that...

1117
01:04:16,395 --> 01:04:20,023
Something that'll work in your favor, Colonel.

1118
01:04:20,148 --> 01:04:22,067
(Kenneth)
Glad to hear you say that.

1119
01:04:22,192 --> 01:04:25,862
A person's fortune is something you draw in.

1120
01:04:34,663 --> 01:04:37,833
(Liaison A) There were ground troops aboard the carrier,

1121
01:04:38,500 --> 01:04:41,086
It seems Man Hunter came in on today's flight, too.

1122
01:04:41,211 --> 01:04:43,130
What about the Man Hunter disturbance in Davao?

1123
01:04:43,255 --> 01:04:44,298
(Hathaway) I've heard.

1124
01:04:44,423 --> 01:04:47,175
(Liaison B) There were quite a few of them,
and Hong Kong types as well.

1125
01:04:47,301 --> 01:04:50,429
The order to reinforce Kowloon's security

1126
01:04:50,554 --> 01:04:52,097
was a lie.

1127
01:04:52,222 --> 01:04:53,181
(Hathaway) Hm...

1128
01:04:53,599 --> 01:04:56,435
(Liaison A) What concerns me is
the large amount of electronics—

1129
01:04:56,560 --> 01:04:59,187
Large equipment is being transported.

1130
01:04:59,313 --> 01:05:02,482
Isn't that for electrical reinforcement
of the conference hall?

1131
01:05:02,608 --> 01:05:05,652
No, Adelaide wasn't hit by a colony drop.

1132
01:05:06,236 --> 01:05:08,530
There shouldn't be any need
for large-scale reinforcement.

1133
01:05:08,530 --> 01:05:08,947
There shouldn't be any need
for large-scale reinforcement
(propeller noise)

1134
01:05:08,947 --> 01:05:09,072
(propeller noise)

1135
01:05:09,072 --> 01:05:10,115
(propeller noise)
(Member A) Hey, look!

1136
01:05:10,240 --> 01:05:11,533
(Member A) It's here!
(Member B) What is it?

1137
01:05:16,288 --> 01:05:18,457
(Fabio)
They say a snake knows a snake's path,

1138
01:05:18,582 --> 01:05:20,876
To think we could meet up in a place like this.

1139
01:05:21,001 --> 01:05:22,628
So? What is it?

1140
01:05:23,837 --> 01:05:24,630
(Fabio) Hmph...

1141
01:05:25,130 --> 01:05:28,508
There are plenty of Base Jabbers sitting right there, boss!

1142
01:05:28,634 --> 01:05:30,260
Can we borrow a couple?

1143
01:05:30,385 --> 01:05:33,972
Then taking Darwin Airport would be easy.

1144
01:05:34,097 --> 01:05:35,932
(Hathaway)
A ride to Kowloon?

1145
01:05:36,391 --> 01:05:37,184
Heh.

1146
01:05:37,309 --> 01:05:39,019
Not Kowloon?

1147
01:05:39,144 --> 01:05:42,105
(Hathaway)
Adelaide. It's solid intel.

1148
01:05:42,230 --> 01:05:43,273
Hah...

1149
01:05:43,649 --> 01:05:45,400
So the ones we had lying low in Darwin...

1150
01:05:45,525 --> 01:05:47,611
were all for nothing...

1151
01:05:48,028 --> 01:05:49,946
(Hathaway)
What do you say we keep going?

1152
01:05:50,072 --> 01:05:52,574
(Fabio)
Why? I thought we weren't going to Ko Chang.

1153
01:05:52,699 --> 01:05:53,659
(Hathaway)
Iram.

1154
01:05:53,992 --> 01:05:57,287
(Iram)
In other words, if you'll attack
Darwin for us,

1155
01:05:57,412 --> 01:05:59,498
we can make it look like Mafty forces
are moving to Ko Chang.

1156
01:05:59,623 --> 01:06:00,916
We can create that impression.

1157
01:06:01,041 --> 01:06:04,586
(Fabio)
So you're making it look like
you fell for the diversion, then?

1158
01:06:04,711 --> 01:06:05,504
(Hathaway)
That's right.

1159
01:06:05,629 --> 01:06:08,465
(Chang)
If we use the men standing by at the port,

1160
01:06:08,590 --> 01:06:10,509
we can attack Darwin right away.

1161
01:06:10,634 --> 01:06:13,136
If you'll give us ten portable
missile launchers,

1162
01:06:13,261 --> 01:06:15,389
we'll make it a success.

1163
01:06:15,806 --> 01:06:16,932
(Iram)
I'll have them prepared.

1164
01:06:17,057 --> 01:06:19,601
(Fabio)
But what about compensation after that?

1165
01:06:19,935 --> 01:06:21,186
(Hathaway)
The problem of food supply—

1166
01:06:21,311 --> 01:06:23,522
you'll have to negotiate
with Quack Salver.

1167
01:06:24,231 --> 01:06:26,316
Will you help them with that?

1168
01:06:26,441 --> 01:06:27,734
All right.

1169
01:06:27,859 --> 01:06:30,904
Fabio, there are all sorts
of Mafty restrictions, but...

1170
01:06:31,029 --> 01:06:32,823
I hope you can accept that.

1171
01:06:32,948 --> 01:06:35,450
(Fabio)
Yeah, I know that in my bones.

1172
01:06:38,161 --> 01:06:39,538
(distant thunder)

1173
01:06:39,663 --> 01:06:40,455
(Hathaway)
Julia.

1174
01:06:41,915 --> 01:06:42,708
Hasa.

1175
01:06:42,833 --> 01:06:44,793
(Hathaway)
You're staying on the Valiant?

1176
01:06:44,918 --> 01:06:46,753
(Julia)
The Xi's maintenance is done,

1177
01:06:46,878 --> 01:06:49,047
and what happens after Adelaide
matters too.

1178
01:06:49,172 --> 01:06:51,425
(Hathaway)
Besides, even if you don't make the rounds...

1179
01:06:53,051 --> 01:06:54,970
I get along with that girl pretty well.

1180
01:06:56,805 --> 01:07:00,308
But you know, Hasa, you push
Mafty too hard,

1181
01:07:00,434 --> 01:07:02,310
and I feel sorry for Kelia.

1182
01:07:02,436 --> 01:07:04,020
(Hathaway)
It can't be helped...

1183
01:07:05,230 --> 01:07:06,982
(Julia)
I think she's still around.

1184
01:07:07,399 --> 01:07:08,316
(Hathaway)
Huh?

1185
01:07:08,442 --> 01:07:10,402
(Julia)
She came with the liaison, didn't she?

1186
01:07:10,861 --> 01:07:12,612
I was told not to say, but...

1187
01:07:13,280 --> 01:07:14,322
That girl

1188
01:07:14,448 --> 01:07:16,867
said she's leaving Mafty
once this is over.

1189
01:07:17,159 --> 01:07:17,951
(Hathaway)
Ah!

1190
01:07:18,076 --> 01:07:18,535
(running footsteps)

1191
01:07:18,535 --> 01:07:20,203
(running footsteps)
She said, 'Survive...'

1192
01:07:22,831 --> 01:07:23,331
(Hathaway breathing heavily)

1193
01:07:23,331 --> 01:07:26,460
(Hathaway breathing heavily)
♪～

1194
01:07:26,460 --> 01:07:28,295
♪～

1195
01:07:33,175 --> 01:07:34,009
(Hathaway, voiceover)
Why

1196
01:07:35,594 --> 01:07:36,386
run?

1197
01:07:36,511 --> 01:07:37,929
♪ Look

1198
01:07:38,054 --> 01:07:39,848
♪ again

1199
01:07:39,973 --> 01:07:43,310
♪ falling down

1200
01:07:43,435 --> 01:07:44,978
♪ rain

1201
01:07:45,103 --> 01:07:48,523
♪ Fading away

1202
01:07:48,648 --> 01:07:50,192
♪ Sound

1203
01:07:50,317 --> 01:07:56,948
♪ No matter how much I scream

1204
01:07:57,073 --> 01:08:02,621
♪ Because it won't reach you

1205
01:08:03,997 --> 01:08:07,167
♪ We'd already gone

1206
01:08:07,292 --> 01:08:10,587
♪ Even if I unravel it, weakness

1207
01:08:11,004 --> 01:08:13,507
♪ A searching voice

1208
01:08:14,007 --> 01:08:18,428
♪ Runs like a revolving lantern, over and over

1209
01:08:18,553 --> 01:08:20,222
♪ Gazing

1210
01:08:20,347 --> 01:08:21,973
♪ Drowning

1211
01:08:22,098 --> 01:08:25,352
♪ Even if my heart withers

1212
01:08:25,477 --> 01:08:28,688
♪ The two of us turn into the past

1213
01:08:29,064 --> 01:08:32,526
♪ Someone's gotta go

1214
01:08:39,991 --> 01:08:41,618
♪ No light

1215
01:08:41,743 --> 01:08:43,662
♪ At the end of

1216
01:08:43,787 --> 01:08:46,832
♪ This hollow

1217
01:08:46,957 --> 01:08:48,375
♪ Wind

1218
01:08:48,500 --> 01:08:51,795
♪ Growing clear

1219
01:08:51,920 --> 01:08:53,171
♪ Left brain

1220
01:08:53,630 --> 01:09:00,512
♪ No matter how much I scream

1221
01:09:00,637 --> 01:09:05,517
♪ But it won't reach you

1222
01:09:07,227 --> 01:09:10,814
♪ We'd already gone

1223
01:09:10,939 --> 01:09:14,276
♪ Even if I unravel it, weakness

1224
01:09:14,651 --> 01:09:17,404
♪ A searching voice

1225
01:09:17,529 --> 01:09:21,992
♪ Runs like a revolving lantern, over and over

1226
01:09:22,117 --> 01:09:23,577
♪ Gazing

1227
01:09:23,702 --> 01:09:25,203
♪ Drowning

1228
01:09:25,328 --> 01:09:28,874
♪ Even if my heart withers

1229
01:09:28,999 --> 01:09:32,419
♪ The two of us turn into the past

1230
01:09:32,544 --> 01:09:37,173
♪ Someone's gotta go

1231
01:09:47,183 --> 01:09:49,644
(Kenneth) Gigi. Gigi.

1232
01:09:53,481 --> 01:09:56,484
(noise inside the aircraft)

1233
01:09:56,610 --> 01:09:57,736
(noise subsides)

1234
01:09:57,861 --> 01:09:59,446
(Kenneth)
We'll be in Darwin soon.

1235
01:09:59,571 --> 01:10:00,363
(Gigi) Hm...?

1236
01:10:00,488 --> 01:10:02,741
It turned out exactly as Gigi said.

1237
01:10:02,866 --> 01:10:05,243
We sank one of Mafty's ships.

1238
01:10:05,744 --> 01:10:06,995
Really, Colonel!?

1239
01:10:07,120 --> 01:10:10,415
(Kenneth) Yes. It's the ship we call M-3.

1240
01:10:10,540 --> 01:10:11,541
I see!

1241
01:10:11,666 --> 01:10:14,920
That will thin out Mafty's supply lines considerably.

1242
01:10:15,045 --> 01:10:18,131
Yes. She—Gigi Andalusia—

1243
01:10:18,256 --> 01:10:20,258
predicted this victory for us.

1244
01:10:20,383 --> 01:10:21,593
(Minecche) I see...

1245
01:10:21,718 --> 01:10:23,011
(Wave)
I've heard the rumors...

1246
01:10:23,136 --> 01:10:26,765
(Kenneth) Well... whether you believe it or not is up to you.

1247
01:10:26,890 --> 01:10:30,894
As your commander, I'll take any good omen I can get.

1248
01:10:50,413 --> 01:10:51,665
(Gigi) I don't want to get off...

1249
01:10:55,293 --> 01:10:56,836
I hate this airport...!

1250
01:10:56,962 --> 01:10:57,796
(Kenneth) Ah!

1251
01:10:59,881 --> 01:11:01,925
Nn... ugh...

1252
01:11:02,592 --> 01:11:03,593
Abort landing!

1253
01:11:03,718 --> 01:11:05,345
(Officer A) Huh? Right now?

1254
01:11:05,470 --> 01:11:07,013
(Kenneth) Launch aircraft 1 and 2 as well.

1255
01:11:07,138 --> 01:11:08,390
(Officer A) But...
(Kenneth) Hurry!!

1256
01:11:29,077 --> 01:11:31,371
(Copilot) What's wrong? Respond.

1257
01:11:31,496 --> 01:11:33,289
We've lost contact.

1258
01:11:33,415 --> 01:11:35,250
(Officer B)
Could it be a Mafty surprise attack...?

1259
01:11:35,750 --> 01:11:37,961
(Officer A) The Maftys heading for Kowloon...

1260
01:11:38,086 --> 01:11:39,879
Could they have raided Darwin!?

1261
01:11:40,422 --> 01:11:44,300
(Kenneth) They don't have the transport capacity
to carry ground troops.

1262
01:11:44,801 --> 01:11:47,929
That's probably what they wanted...

1263
01:11:52,017 --> 01:11:54,310
What does it feel like?

1264
01:11:54,436 --> 01:11:55,228
(Gigi) Hm?

1265
01:11:55,353 --> 01:11:57,272
(Minecche) Like you see images?

1266
01:11:57,397 --> 01:11:59,315
(Gigi) No, how should I put it...

1267
01:11:59,441 --> 01:12:01,860
It's not something that clear...

1268
01:12:01,985 --> 01:12:03,653
More like a vague bad feeling...

1269
01:12:03,778 --> 01:12:07,490
(Officer B) Colonel, things like this really do happen.

1270
01:12:07,615 --> 01:12:08,491
(Kenneth) What?

1271
01:12:08,616 --> 01:12:10,910
(Officer B) It's an omen, sir. An omen.

1272
01:12:11,036 --> 01:12:13,079
There really are people who bring
that kind of thing with them.

1273
01:12:13,204 --> 01:12:15,206
That's what I'm saying.

1274
01:12:15,331 --> 01:12:16,916
(Kenneth) You mean me?

1275
01:12:17,459 --> 01:12:19,544
(Officer B)
Yes, yes! Exactly.

1276
01:12:19,669 --> 01:12:21,713
You're the one who called her here,
aren't you, Colonel?

1277
01:12:21,838 --> 01:12:23,840
Gigi Andalucia.

1278
01:12:36,770 --> 01:12:38,688
(ringing)

1279
01:12:41,107 --> 01:12:44,527
(McGovern) So, did the Director see the footage?

1280
01:12:44,652 --> 01:12:45,570
(Yeoksan) Of course.

1281
01:12:45,695 --> 01:12:48,907
That would completely undermine
the Federation government's prestige.

1282
01:12:49,741 --> 01:12:54,079
The Kimberley unit's mobile suits
grabbing a person and crushing them—

1283
01:12:54,204 --> 01:12:56,539
The public must never see that.

1284
01:12:56,998 --> 01:12:59,292
(Yeoksan)
I am fully aware of that.

1285
01:12:59,417 --> 01:13:03,171
We'll take steps against the station
that aired that video.

1286
01:13:03,296 --> 01:13:06,508
(McGovern)
SPTV is a tough network.

1287
01:13:06,633 --> 01:13:09,219
That chairman must have a weakness.

1288
01:13:09,344 --> 01:13:11,846
(McGovern) In any case, stop that news immediately.

1289
01:13:12,388 --> 01:13:14,641
I want nothing more to do with this.

1290
01:13:14,766 --> 01:13:17,644
(Yeoksan) Of course.
I will forget it as well.

1291
01:13:17,769 --> 01:13:19,062
(McGovern) That's best.

1292
01:13:19,813 --> 01:13:20,855
(Yeoksan) Well?

1293
01:13:20,980 --> 01:13:23,525
(Female Secretary) The Information and Communications Ministry
will take action, but...

1294
01:13:23,650 --> 01:13:24,776
It will take time...

1295
01:13:24,901 --> 01:13:27,737
(Yeoksan)
What about my appointment with the Deputy Chief
of the General Staff?

1296
01:13:27,862 --> 01:13:30,156
(Hugest)
He says he can see you right now.

1297
01:13:30,281 --> 01:13:31,324
(Yeoksan) What floor is he on?

1298
01:13:31,449 --> 01:13:32,909
(Hugest) The top floor.

1299
01:13:34,119 --> 01:13:36,246
(Yeoksan)
This isn't rural Davao.

1300
01:13:36,621 --> 01:13:40,375
If you want to keep seeing this view,
be more careful.

1301
01:13:40,500 --> 01:13:41,417
(Hugest) Yes...?

1302
01:13:43,044 --> 01:13:46,089
(Hugest) The hijacking was planned by Fabio Rivera.

1303
01:13:46,214 --> 01:13:48,842
The ones who had gathered at Oenpelli.

1304
01:13:48,967 --> 01:13:51,177
They seem to be a group inspired by Mafty.

1305
01:13:51,719 --> 01:13:54,055
(Gigi) Just do it!
They're fakes!

1306
01:13:54,639 --> 01:13:57,350
Just as that girl suspected...

1307
01:13:58,059 --> 01:14:01,312
(Hugest) What should we do about tracking and apprehending the people involved?

1308
01:14:01,437 --> 01:14:04,274
(Yeoksan) Bright Noa's son, huh...

1309
01:14:04,941 --> 01:14:08,194
Stand down. Reassign the personnel to Adelaide security.

1310
01:14:08,319 --> 01:14:09,237
(Hugest) Understood.

1311
01:14:13,408 --> 01:14:15,451
(Revye) Man, I just got here

1312
01:14:15,869 --> 01:14:18,538
and this is before I've even had a shower.

1313
01:14:24,252 --> 01:14:26,087
When does the minister arrive?

1314
01:14:26,212 --> 01:14:28,381
(Revye) Yes, tonight if nothing unusual.

1315
01:14:29,299 --> 01:14:31,718
(Yeoksan) You know Kenneth's Kirke unit, don't you?

1316
01:14:31,843 --> 01:14:33,803
(Revye) Yes. Tomorrow morning, I hear

1317
01:14:33,928 --> 01:14:36,848
he'll be arriving here in person.

1318
01:14:37,473 --> 01:14:39,475
(Yeoksan) They've been having a rough time too.

1319
01:14:39,601 --> 01:14:42,896
The cabinet ministers only think about their own safety

1320
01:14:43,021 --> 01:14:45,690
and keep making unreasonable demands on them.

1321
01:14:45,815 --> 01:14:46,941
(Revye) So it seems.

1322
01:14:47,650 --> 01:14:49,694
(Yeoksan) ...So, what do you think?

1323
01:14:49,819 --> 01:14:50,612
(Revye) About what?

1324
01:14:50,737 --> 01:14:52,947
(Yeoksan) About providing cover for the Kirke unit.

1325
01:14:53,615 --> 01:14:55,867
The reason they bungled things at Oenpelli

1326
01:14:55,992 --> 01:14:57,994
isn't just a problem with the commander.

1327
01:14:58,119 --> 01:15:00,121
It's an organizational problem.

1328
01:15:00,246 --> 01:15:01,080
Understand?

1329
01:15:01,206 --> 01:15:04,417
We need someone with real combat experience immediately.

1330
01:15:05,001 --> 01:15:08,171
Bright Noa of the Independent 13th Unit

1331
01:15:08,296 --> 01:15:12,050
is a young commander with extensive combat experience, I'd say...

1332
01:15:12,175 --> 01:15:13,676
(Revye) I'll look into it.

1333
01:15:20,642 --> 01:15:27,607
(combat sounds)

1334
01:15:28,858 --> 01:15:29,984
(explosion)

1335
01:15:38,368 --> 01:15:40,078
(Iram) What's burning?

1336
01:15:48,336 --> 01:15:49,545
(Hathaway) A pile of garbage.

1337
01:15:49,671 --> 01:15:51,089
(Iram) How did it catch fire...?

1338
01:15:55,885 --> 01:15:57,220
(Hathaway) It's Hala's mobile suit.

1339
01:15:59,305 --> 01:16:00,139
Hm...

1340
01:16:00,598 --> 01:16:02,850
(Iram) Rod and Hendrix should be with Hala.

1341
01:16:11,985 --> 01:16:14,237
(Iram) We'd better assume it's the enemy's movement route.

1342
01:16:14,362 --> 01:16:15,154
Let's go.

1343
01:16:28,001 --> 01:16:29,335
(Iram) It's around here.

1344
01:16:31,754 --> 01:16:33,089
(electronic beep)

1345
01:16:34,424 --> 01:16:35,383
(Iram) There it is!

1346
01:16:44,225 --> 01:16:45,768
(bird chirping)
(Hathaway) Whoa!

1347
01:16:49,564 --> 01:16:51,065
(Hathaway) Then Rod, too...

1348
01:16:51,482 --> 01:16:55,570
(Hendrix) I'm sorry...
I couldn't save them...

1349
01:16:55,695 --> 01:16:57,155
(Hathaway) You shook off the enemy pursuit

1350
01:16:57,280 --> 01:17:01,034
and made it here. That alone is remarkable, Hendrix.

1351
01:17:01,159 --> 01:17:02,952
(Hendrix)
Thank you...

1352
01:17:16,424 --> 01:17:17,967
(Hathaway) The Valiant...

1353
01:17:18,092 --> 01:17:20,887
(Iram) Why do the good ones
always die first?

1354
01:17:21,012 --> 01:17:22,972
(Raymond) Doesn't mean he's dead.

1355
01:17:23,097 --> 01:17:26,517
(Maximilian) Even the Federation
wouldn't kill a man for fleeing a sinking ship.

1356
01:17:26,642 --> 01:17:28,102
(Emeralda) That's right...

1357
01:17:28,227 --> 01:17:31,022
Besides,
it's not all bad...

1358
01:17:31,397 --> 01:17:33,733
I hear Fabio Rivera
pulled it off well.

1359
01:17:33,858 --> 01:17:35,818
(Hathaway) I see. He pulled it off.

1360
01:17:35,943 --> 01:17:37,779
(Iram) You've got good friends.

1361
01:17:37,904 --> 01:17:38,780
(Hathaway) Yeah...

1362
01:17:43,826 --> 01:17:45,620
(Hathaway) I wonder if Gawman
and the others are doing all right.

1363
01:17:45,745 --> 01:17:49,165
(Iram) You get some sleep first.
I'll go check on a few things.

1364
01:17:49,290 --> 01:17:50,375
(Hathaway) Please.

1365
01:17:54,295 --> 01:17:55,088
(door closes)

1366
01:17:58,132 --> 01:17:59,884
(Hathaway) It was just awful...

1367
01:18:00,551 --> 01:18:01,386
Right?

1368
01:18:02,053 --> 01:18:02,720
Quess.

1369
01:18:09,477 --> 01:18:11,354
Compared to this...

1370
01:18:11,479 --> 01:18:14,982
Kelia was nothing more than
a trivial worldly act.

1371
01:18:15,400 --> 01:18:16,859
And as for Gigi...

1372
01:18:18,861 --> 01:18:19,654
It's a disgrace...

1373
01:18:27,537 --> 01:18:29,330
Hah! Ah!

1374
01:18:29,664 --> 01:18:31,958
Ahhh... Ahhh!

1375
01:18:32,083 --> 01:18:35,378
Ah! Ah! Ugh...

1376
01:18:53,187 --> 01:18:54,981
(Minecche)
Your luggage arrived ahead of you.

1377
01:18:55,106 --> 01:18:56,899
How fortunate.

1378
01:18:57,442 --> 01:18:59,902
(Gigi) Where will the colonel
be sleeping?

1379
01:19:00,027 --> 01:19:02,572
(Minecche) He has work again tonight,
so he'll be up late.

1380
01:19:02,697 --> 01:19:05,741
He's on that floor
where the lights are on.

1381
01:19:06,576 --> 01:19:09,787
This entire area has been
requisitioned by the military.

1382
01:19:09,912 --> 01:19:11,956
Except for running errands
for your boyfriend.

1383
01:19:12,081 --> 01:19:15,168
The hotel shouldn't complain either. Heh heh.

1384
01:19:16,252 --> 01:19:17,086
Heh heh.

1385
01:19:17,211 --> 01:19:18,171
(Gigi) Thank you.

1386
01:19:18,713 --> 01:19:20,840
(Minecche)
...And what do you think?

1387
01:19:21,174 --> 01:19:23,885
Do you sense what lies ahead?

1388
01:19:24,343 --> 01:19:27,430
(Gigi)
Let's see... Well, all will be fine...

1389
01:19:27,555 --> 01:19:28,556
Oh-ho-ho!

1390
01:19:28,681 --> 01:19:32,101
But I'm not a prophet, you know.

1391
01:19:32,226 --> 01:19:33,686
Yes, I understand.

1392
01:19:34,187 --> 01:19:36,272
Please rest well tonight.

1393
01:19:36,397 --> 01:19:39,442
Please show me
that new power again sometime.

1394
01:19:50,369 --> 01:19:53,789
(Gigi, voiceover) Things are
a little off.

1395
01:19:54,373 --> 01:19:58,294
I think today's events
were just the colonel's luck.

1396
01:19:58,419 --> 01:20:01,797
He's a capable commander.

1397
01:20:02,215 --> 01:20:06,010
He does prepare
where you can't see it.

1398
01:20:06,594 --> 01:20:09,931
Hathaway and the others
are the ones improvising.

1399
01:20:10,348 --> 01:20:14,393
He's always struggling,
standing on tiptoe.

1400
01:20:20,274 --> 01:20:22,527
(Cardeas)
There's something I left undone...

1401
01:20:22,902 --> 01:20:25,613
 There is something I must do.

1402
01:20:25,738 --> 01:20:26,864
 (Secretary) Please wait.

1403
01:20:26,989 --> 01:20:28,241
 (Sons) Father!

1404
01:20:29,242 --> 01:20:29,992
 (Son) Move.

1405
01:20:30,701 --> 01:20:32,161
 (Gigi, voiceover) How sad…

1406
01:20:32,620 --> 01:20:35,623
Until death,
plagued by succession and inheritance.

1407
01:20:35,748 --> 01:20:39,293
A man everyone
hopes will die soon…

1408
01:20:43,839 --> 01:20:45,174
It's decided…

1409
01:20:48,594 --> 01:20:51,264
I have a father complex…

1410
01:20:52,348 --> 01:20:53,266
 (Kenneth) Gigi!

1411
01:20:53,391 --> 01:20:54,183
 (Gigi) Huh…

1412
01:20:56,519 --> 01:20:57,645
 (Kenneth) It's a nice room.

1413
01:20:58,563 --> 01:21:00,940
Who'd have thought a hotel like this
would remain here.

1414
01:21:01,065 --> 01:21:02,108
We got lucky.

1415
01:21:02,525 --> 01:21:03,317
Ah…

1416
01:21:03,901 --> 01:21:04,986
 (Gigi) It is.

1417
01:21:08,239 --> 01:21:09,240
Let's head out…

1418
01:21:10,700 --> 01:21:12,451
Among the top officials
of the Federation government,

1419
01:21:12,577 --> 01:21:15,121
there are those who own tens of thousands
of acres of land around here

1420
01:21:15,246 --> 01:21:17,748
under their own names, apparently.

1421
01:21:18,332 --> 01:21:19,625
 (Gigi) What's that?

1422
01:21:19,750 --> 01:21:21,252
Status!

1423
01:21:21,377 --> 01:21:24,255
It's what people ultimately desire.

1424
01:21:24,380 --> 01:21:27,800
That means those kinds of people
are inside the government.

1425
01:21:27,925 --> 01:21:31,304
Oh, gross.
Why do adults end up like that?

1426
01:21:31,721 --> 01:21:33,472
 (Kenneth) Though humans are animals,

1427
01:21:33,598 --> 01:21:37,685
the heart desires to exist
outside the cycle of life and death.

1428
01:21:37,810 --> 01:21:39,186
I see…

1429
01:21:39,312 --> 01:21:41,856
 (Kenneth) But
that it is eternal—

1430
01:21:41,981 --> 01:21:44,567
there's no guarantee of that
in the real world.

1431
01:21:45,985 --> 01:21:49,488
What can a person take with them when they die?

1432
01:21:50,156 --> 01:21:53,117
 (Gigi, voiceover)
Do what you can only do while young.

1433
01:21:53,242 --> 01:21:55,995
That's why I'm going.

1434
01:21:58,039 --> 01:21:58,998
 (Gigi) Colonel.

1435
01:21:59,832 --> 01:22:02,460
Do you know anything
about Colonel Heyman?

1436
01:22:02,835 --> 01:22:04,629
 (Kenneth) What's wrong?
All of a sudden…

1437
01:22:04,754 --> 01:22:07,214
I just hope the Kirke unit's
last unresolved issue

1438
01:22:07,340 --> 01:22:09,383
gets resolved…

1439
01:22:09,508 --> 01:22:11,052
 (Kenneth) You say the strangest things.

1440
01:22:11,177 --> 01:22:12,178
 (Gigi) Near here,

1441
01:22:12,303 --> 01:22:14,305
there's a place called Ayers Rock,
isn't there?

1442
01:22:15,514 --> 01:22:16,307
Tomorrow morning,

1443
01:22:16,974 --> 01:22:20,269
I wonder if I can see it
before we leave.

1444
01:22:20,561 --> 01:22:21,354
I want to do some sightseeing.

1445
01:22:21,854 --> 01:22:24,398
Does this have something to do
with Kimberley?

1446
01:22:24,523 --> 01:22:25,608
 (Gigi) I don't know.

1447
01:22:25,733 --> 01:22:28,319
It just came to me.

1448
01:22:33,074 --> 01:22:36,202
 (Kimberley) This is Air Force Commander
Kimberley Heyman.

1449
01:22:36,577 --> 01:22:38,788
We will, from the South Pacific airspace,

1450
01:22:38,913 --> 01:22:41,415
achieve the complete elimination
of anti-Federation forces.

1451
01:22:41,874 --> 01:22:44,418
Keep in step with the Criminal Police Organization...

1452
01:22:44,960 --> 01:22:46,921
(Mira) To Earth? When?

1453
01:22:47,046 --> 01:22:49,799
(Bright)
I'm leaving early in the morning
the day after tomorrow.

1454
01:22:49,924 --> 01:22:51,592
(Mira) That day, we're going
to New Hampshire Sea.

1455
01:22:51,717 --> 01:22:53,344
to see a shop...

1456
01:22:53,469 --> 01:22:57,348
(Bright) That's true, but...
Couldn't you go tomorrow instead?

1457
01:22:57,473 --> 01:23:00,768
(Mira) Did you really
submit your resignation to the military?

1458
01:23:00,893 --> 01:23:01,686
(Bright) Yeah.

1459
01:23:02,603 --> 01:23:04,230
I got a promise
that this will be the last time.

1460
01:23:04,230 --> 01:23:05,564
I got a promise
that this will be the last time
(phone ringing)

1461
01:23:06,732 --> 01:23:08,192
(Mira) Yes... that's right.

1462
01:23:08,317 --> 01:23:11,737
About the lakefront tenant viewing
the day after tomorrow...

1463
01:23:12,905 --> 01:23:15,366
Would first thing
tomorrow afternoon work?

1464
01:23:15,741 --> 01:23:17,159
Can you spare the time?

1465
01:23:17,284 --> 01:23:18,577
(Bright) I'll make time!

1466
01:23:18,703 --> 01:23:18,911
I'll make the higher-ups agree to it.

1467
01:23:18,911 --> 01:23:21,122
I'll make the higher-ups agree to it.
(Mira) That's fine.
Please go ahead.

1468
01:23:21,122 --> 01:23:21,872
(Mira) That's fine.
Please go ahead.

1469
01:23:22,331 --> 01:23:25,042
(Mira)
Was the Oenpelli matter the direct cause?

1470
01:23:25,167 --> 01:23:26,544
(Bright) I suppose so...

1471
01:23:26,669 --> 01:23:28,838
Even though you have
military force like an elephant

1472
01:23:28,963 --> 01:23:30,798
if they swarm around you
like ants

1473
01:23:30,923 --> 01:23:33,300
how you should control
your own power

1474
01:23:33,801 --> 01:23:35,302
is a difficult problem.

1475
01:23:35,428 --> 01:23:36,804
(Mira) Well, that's true...

1476
01:23:45,563 --> 01:23:46,397
(sound of a kiss)

1477
01:23:47,648 --> 01:23:50,151
(Mira) You may get to see Hathaway.

1478
01:23:50,276 --> 01:23:52,194
(Bright)
Yeah... once the operation's over,

1479
01:23:52,319 --> 01:23:54,947
the island where he's doing
plant fieldwork—

1480
01:23:55,072 --> 01:23:56,198
I'll try to stop by.

1481
01:23:56,866 --> 01:23:58,409
(Mira) What about dinner tonight?

1482
01:23:58,743 --> 01:24:00,286
(Bright)
No, but I'll definitely come home.

1483
01:24:00,411 --> 01:24:02,705
(Mira)
I see... take care.

1484
01:24:16,177 --> 01:24:19,472
(Kenneth) Listen up!
A Mafty deployment is possible.

1485
01:24:19,597 --> 01:24:22,391
At a place as conspicuous
as Ayers Rock,

1486
01:24:22,516 --> 01:24:25,561
we never imagined Mafty
would be hiding there,

1487
01:24:25,686 --> 01:24:28,397
but she showed us
that possibility!

1488
01:24:28,522 --> 01:24:29,690
Don't let your guard down!

1489
01:24:29,815 --> 01:24:30,816
(Pilots) Sir!

1490
01:24:31,192 --> 01:24:33,444
(Kenneth)
They're veterans you can trust.

1491
01:24:33,569 --> 01:24:34,361
What's that?

1492
01:24:34,487 --> 01:24:35,863
(Gigi) While watching the sunrise,

1493
01:24:35,988 --> 01:24:37,990
we all have breakfast together.

1494
01:24:38,699 --> 01:24:41,160
(Kenneth) I'll arrange lunch
in Adelaide.

1495
01:24:42,077 --> 01:24:44,079
(Gigi) I'm counting on you, Colonel.

1496
01:24:44,371 --> 01:24:45,706
(Wave) Ms. Gigi! Here you go.

1497
01:24:48,417 --> 01:24:51,003
(Minecche)
Colonel, you need to hurry.

1498
01:24:51,128 --> 01:24:52,254
(Kenneth) I know.

1499
01:24:55,633 --> 01:24:57,760
(Lane's Mechanic B)
He came up through the technical track—

1500
01:24:57,885 --> 01:25:00,137
That's how a senile colonel does things.

1501
01:25:01,180 --> 01:25:04,183
(Lane, voiceover)
That alone shows how much this unit's existence...

1502
01:25:04,308 --> 01:25:07,561
The world of the adults
running this unit

1503
01:25:07,686 --> 01:25:09,814
is warped.

1504
01:25:11,816 --> 01:25:15,194
There's no way Mafty
would be at a tourist spot!

1505
01:25:18,823 --> 01:25:20,324
I don't believe it.

1506
01:25:21,325 --> 01:25:22,451
Damn it!

1507
01:25:31,418 --> 01:25:32,378
(Mechanic) Ms. Gigi.

1508
01:25:33,546 --> 01:25:34,880
It's in sight.

1509
01:25:39,260 --> 01:25:41,178
(Gigi) That's Ayers Rock...

1510
01:25:53,274 --> 01:25:54,775
(Lowaist) All hands, evacuate!

1511
01:25:55,234 --> 01:25:57,403
We're heading for the wall, as planned!

1512
01:25:57,528 --> 01:25:58,654
(Hathaway) Lo!

1513
01:25:58,779 --> 01:26:00,573
(Hathaway) See you!
(Raymond) We're counting on you!

1514
01:26:01,115 --> 01:26:01,907
(Hathaway) Ready?

1515
01:26:02,283 --> 01:26:04,118
(Lowaist)
The connect area is tight.

1516
01:26:04,243 --> 01:26:05,703
I've sent the position to Maxi.

1517
01:26:06,287 --> 01:26:07,413
(Hathaway) Sorry...

1518
01:26:08,247 --> 01:26:10,875
(Lowaist) The rear guard
never says 'sorry.'

1519
01:26:11,417 --> 01:26:13,085
(Maximilian)
The positions are already registered.

1520
01:26:13,210 --> 01:26:14,753
You can do it!

1521
01:26:14,879 --> 01:26:16,130
(Hathaway) I hope so.

1522
01:26:16,255 --> 01:26:18,674
(Fabio)
Hey, Mafty!

1523
01:26:19,133 --> 01:26:19,925
You all right?

1524
01:26:20,050 --> 01:26:21,844
(Hathaway)
I'll hold them off! Go!

1525
01:26:21,969 --> 01:26:24,805
(Fabio)
Yeah! Don't you die on me!

1526
01:26:30,269 --> 01:26:32,688
(Lowaist) Two enemy units!
One Base Jabber!

1527
01:26:32,813 --> 01:26:34,815
All Galcezon units,
maintain low altitude

1528
01:26:34,940 --> 01:26:37,151
Use Ayers Rock as cover
and proceed southwest.

1529
01:26:37,276 --> 01:26:38,068
(Hathaway) So this is it...

1530
01:26:38,694 --> 01:26:40,154
(Lowaist)
The remote control's sensitivity is tight.

1531
01:26:40,279 --> 01:26:42,406
Comm range is limited. In other words...

1532
01:26:42,531 --> 01:26:45,326
(Hathaway) I get close, lock on,
and fire.

1533
01:26:45,451 --> 01:26:46,410
(Lowaist) Exactly!

1534
01:26:46,535 --> 01:26:47,328
(Hathaway) I'll give it a try!

1535
01:26:47,453 --> 01:26:48,579
(Lowaist) All right! Withdraw!

1536
01:26:48,704 --> 01:26:50,372
(Hathaway) I'll overcome them—

1537
01:26:50,497 --> 01:26:51,248
the mundane world,

1538
01:26:52,041 --> 01:26:53,292
and carnal desire!!

1539
01:27:08,182 --> 01:27:09,350
(Gigi) Ahh!

1540
01:27:11,727 --> 01:27:13,562
(Hathaway)
It really is that simple...

1541
01:27:30,746 --> 01:27:31,538
(alarm)

1542
01:27:38,712 --> 01:27:39,505
(alarm)

1543
01:27:41,465 --> 01:27:42,174
(Hathaway) What?!

1544
01:27:50,432 --> 01:27:51,350
(Hathaway) Impressive!

1545
01:27:57,314 --> 01:27:58,148
(alarm)

1546
01:28:13,872 --> 01:28:14,999
(Gigi) Uhhh...

1547
01:28:28,846 --> 01:28:30,681
(alarm)
(Hathaway) Another one!

1548
01:28:46,196 --> 01:28:47,281
(Hathaway) Nn... nnh...

1549
01:28:47,698 --> 01:28:49,825
Nn! A new model?!

1550
01:28:50,659 --> 01:28:51,744
(alarm)

1551
01:28:57,791 --> 01:28:59,043
(rapid gunfire)

1552
01:29:07,926 --> 01:29:09,720
(Hathaway) Uoooaah!

1553
01:29:30,824 --> 01:29:33,202
(Lane)
It's not that I trusted him.

1554
01:29:33,827 --> 01:29:34,787
Not Gigi...

1555
01:29:34,912 --> 01:29:36,789
I sensed it!

1556
01:29:37,372 --> 01:29:38,457
(Hathaway) Lane Aim!?

1557
01:29:45,422 --> 01:29:47,049
(Lane) Ah...

1558
01:29:47,174 --> 01:29:49,426
Ngh! Dammit!!

1559
01:30:02,898 --> 01:30:05,234
(Lane) You fake Gundam!

1560
01:30:22,459 --> 01:30:24,419
(Lane) Only skill matters...

1561
01:30:25,003 --> 01:30:26,880
Luck, predictions...

1562
01:30:27,381 --> 01:30:28,507
As if such things

1563
01:30:35,597 --> 01:30:37,891
could settle it!

1564
01:30:57,661 --> 01:30:58,662
(Lane) Hah!!

1565
01:31:00,080 --> 01:31:01,999
Ngh!! Guh...!

1566
01:31:07,379 --> 01:31:09,590
Ngh!! Whoa!

1567
01:31:11,967 --> 01:31:12,885
(Hathaway) He dodged!

1568
01:31:13,010 --> 01:31:15,512
Lane Aim... Nngh...

1569
01:31:34,406 --> 01:31:35,616
(Lane) Guh!
(Hathaway) But...!

1570
01:31:56,053 --> 01:31:57,888
(rapid gunfire)
(alarm)

1571
01:32:03,894 --> 01:32:05,812
After all,
it's a trainer...

1572
01:32:05,938 --> 01:32:06,688
If I don't pull back, I'll be shot down...

1573
01:32:06,688 --> 01:32:08,106
If I don't pull back, I'll be shot down...
(alarm)

1574
01:32:08,232 --> 01:32:10,067
Ugh!! Ngh!

1575
01:32:24,873 --> 01:32:25,958
(Hathaway) Huh!?

1576
01:32:26,083 --> 01:32:32,923
(heavy breathing)

1577
01:33:07,040 --> 01:33:08,166
(Haro) Haro

1578
01:33:08,292 --> 01:33:10,460
(Amuro)
It's the third one, but take good care of it.

1579
01:33:10,585 --> 01:33:11,670
(Hathaway) Of course!

1580
01:33:15,215 --> 01:33:16,216
(Amuro) Let's go!

1581
01:33:31,189 --> 01:33:32,899
(Lane) You again!

1582
01:33:33,608 --> 01:33:36,862
Hostages, fortune-telling, traps...

1583
01:33:36,987 --> 01:33:38,739
The adults are—!

1584
01:33:42,701 --> 01:33:44,286
(Lane) What are you playing at?!

1585
01:33:44,411 --> 01:33:45,704
(Hathaway) I'm not like you!

1586
01:33:45,829 --> 01:33:47,247
Huh? What?

1587
01:33:47,372 --> 01:33:48,707
(Hathaway) Unlike you,

1588
01:33:49,082 --> 01:33:52,127
I'm not just a pilot!

1589
01:33:52,586 --> 01:33:53,879
Amuro Ray!

1590
01:33:54,004 --> 01:33:55,255
(Amuro) If you're so great,

1591
01:33:55,380 --> 01:33:58,342
then use political power
to crush the Federation Government!

1592
01:33:59,718 --> 01:34:02,346
You, who can't take one step
outside the military!

1593
01:34:05,891 --> 01:34:07,267
What are you playing at?

1594
01:34:09,686 --> 01:34:10,979
(Amuro) Hathaway Noa!

1595
01:34:11,104 --> 01:34:14,316
The son of a man who fought
Earth's enemies alongside us—

1596
01:34:14,441 --> 01:34:15,901
Why are you here?!

1597
01:34:16,026 --> 01:34:19,363
Because I've figured out the true nature
of the people who remain on Earth!

1598
01:34:19,488 --> 01:34:22,115
The people who promoted space emigration

1599
01:34:22,240 --> 01:34:25,327
They're monopolizing Earth
all for themselves!

1600
01:34:26,119 --> 01:34:28,914
(Hathaway) Enough to swallow
all of humanity's ego...

1601
01:34:29,039 --> 01:34:31,333
The Earth isn't that big!

1602
01:34:31,458 --> 01:34:34,836
(Amuro) Human wisdom can overcome
something like that.

1603
01:34:34,961 --> 01:34:35,796
Ahh!

1604
01:34:36,630 --> 01:34:38,924
(Hathaway) Then!
Right now—to all you ignorant masses—

1605
01:34:39,049 --> 01:34:40,342
show me you can bestow wisdom!

1606
01:34:40,801 --> 01:34:43,428
(Amuro) That's
his line!

1607
01:34:43,553 --> 01:34:44,888
Hathaway Noa!

1608
01:34:45,972 --> 01:34:48,642
You'd side with the man
who took Quess?!

1609
01:34:48,767 --> 01:34:50,811
(Hathaway) Ah... Quess...

1610
01:35:31,226 --> 01:35:32,686
(Hathaway) Ugh...

1611
01:35:32,811 --> 01:35:35,564
Ugh... stop... ahh... ngh...

1612
01:35:35,689 --> 01:35:37,190
Ugh... ngh...

1613
01:35:39,734 --> 01:35:41,445
(Amuro) Hathaway,
the darkness that dwells within him—

1614
01:35:41,570 --> 01:35:43,780
he's ashamed of that dark part.

1615
01:35:45,323 --> 01:35:46,324
(Both) It's self-loathing.

1616
01:35:46,450 --> 01:35:47,242
(Hathaway) I...

1617
01:35:47,367 --> 01:35:49,828
(Both) When shown kindness,
he felt only humiliation.

1618
01:35:49,953 --> 01:35:50,745
(Hathaway) I—!

1619
01:35:50,871 --> 01:35:52,414
(Both)
But Quack Salver

1620
01:35:52,539 --> 01:35:53,582
shone light on the darkness.

1621
01:35:53,915 --> 01:35:54,708
(Hathaway) Mafty...

1622
01:35:54,833 --> 01:35:56,710
(Both)
It gave his life meaning and purpose.

1623
01:35:56,835 --> 01:35:58,462
(Hathaway) Justice is merciless.

1624
01:35:58,587 --> 01:35:59,754
(Both) Blaming himself,

1625
01:35:59,880 --> 01:36:02,132
he keeps atoning like this,

1626
01:36:02,257 --> 01:36:04,134
fighting evil and injustice.

1627
01:36:04,259 --> 01:36:05,927
(Hathaway) Sometimes sacrifice is necessary.

1628
01:36:06,052 --> 01:36:08,138
(Both)
That's no excuse.

1629
01:36:08,263 --> 01:36:09,055
(Amuro) Hathaway!

1630
01:36:09,181 --> 01:36:10,891
(Hathaway)
Yes, I know.

1631
01:36:11,641 --> 01:36:13,393
That was my fault.

1632
01:36:20,525 --> 01:36:24,696
(rapid gunfire)

1633
01:36:26,239 --> 01:36:28,575
(Hathaway)
Ah... ah... ugh...

1634
01:36:29,868 --> 01:36:30,869
Ngh...

1635
01:36:45,675 --> 01:36:46,551
(Quess) Hathaway?

1636
01:36:47,928 --> 01:36:49,387
(Hathaway)
I must not be forgiven.

1637
01:36:49,513 --> 01:36:50,388
Hathaway!

1638
01:36:50,514 --> 01:36:51,181
(Hathaway) Punish me...

1639
01:36:51,181 --> 01:36:51,515
(Hathaway) Punish me...
(Amuro)
Hathaway Noa!

1640
01:36:51,515 --> 01:36:52,140
(Amuro)
Hathaway Noa!

1641
01:36:52,265 --> 01:36:53,475
Don't say his name, Amuro!

1642
01:36:53,475 --> 01:36:55,644
Don't say his name, Amuro!
(Quess) Ahh!

1643
01:36:55,644 --> 01:36:56,937
(Quess) Ahh!

1644
01:37:00,190 --> 01:37:03,026
(alarm)

1645
01:37:10,909 --> 01:37:13,453
(Lane) Whoa! Aaargh!

1646
01:37:27,008 --> 01:37:27,801
(Lane) Ngh!

1647
01:37:38,687 --> 01:37:40,564
(alarm)
(Lane) Ngh! ...Weapons...

1648
01:37:51,700 --> 01:37:52,534
(Lane) Ngh...

1649
01:38:01,209 --> 01:38:08,049
(Hathaway's breathing)

1650
01:38:08,174 --> 01:38:11,761
(Lane)
Uuh! Ugh... Aaargh!

1651
01:38:12,470 --> 01:38:13,263
(Gigi) That's enough.

1652
01:38:13,388 --> 01:38:14,139
(Hathaway) Hah!

1653
01:38:15,098 --> 01:38:16,516
(incoming transmission beep)
(Pilot) I surrender!

1654
01:38:16,641 --> 01:38:19,102
(Pilot) I won't resist!
Spare my life!

1655
01:38:25,775 --> 01:38:26,568
(Wave) Ms. Gigi!

1656
01:38:27,277 --> 01:38:29,362
I am Gigi Andalucia.

1657
01:38:29,487 --> 01:38:31,197
I am connected to Boundenwood.

1658
01:38:31,906 --> 01:38:33,950
I'll make a good hostage, won't I?

1659
01:38:35,994 --> 01:38:37,621
(Hathaway)
That you are that person—

1660
01:38:37,746 --> 01:38:40,790
We have neither the information nor the means to believe it.

1661
01:38:41,166 --> 01:38:41,958
Then...

1662
01:38:43,084 --> 01:38:44,628
(Gigi) Then you should become a god.

1663
01:38:46,504 --> 01:38:48,006
(Hathaway)
Gigi Andalucia...

1664
01:38:57,974 --> 01:38:59,100
(Hathaway) Is that all?

1665
01:39:08,234 --> 01:39:10,695
(Hathaway) Why... are you here now...?

1666
01:39:14,282 --> 01:39:15,241
(Gigi) Mm!

1667
01:39:31,049 --> 01:39:31,841
Hathaway!

1668
01:39:35,428 --> 01:39:36,888
(Hathaway) Ugh!
(Gigi) Ahh!

1669
01:39:38,932 --> 01:39:41,559
You're the only one wearing one of those!

1670
01:39:45,897 --> 01:39:47,148
(Gigi) Ah...

1671
01:39:49,776 --> 01:39:50,985
(Hathaway) C-Come on!

1672
01:39:51,569 --> 01:39:52,654
(Gigi) Ahh!

1673
01:39:57,367 --> 01:39:59,369
Throw yourself toward me.

1674
01:39:59,494 --> 01:40:01,037
Toward Hathaway...?

1675
01:40:01,162 --> 01:40:03,623
(Hathaway)
That's right. Don't think about anything else.

1676
01:40:03,748 --> 01:40:07,085
Go for it! One, two, three!

1677
01:40:07,210 --> 01:40:08,420
(Gigi) Ahh! Mm...

1678
01:40:08,753 --> 01:40:11,673
Ahh... ahh... Hah... hah...

1679
01:40:13,383 --> 01:40:16,845
(Hathaway)
What are you doing here—of all places?

1680
01:40:19,347 --> 01:40:20,140
(Gigi) Because—!

1681
01:40:20,682 --> 01:40:21,516
(Hathaway) Huh!?

1682
01:40:22,517 --> 01:40:26,646
♪～

1683
01:41:08,229 --> 01:41:11,357
♪ She's got a smile
    that it seems, to me

1684
01:41:11,483 --> 01:41:15,195
♪ Reminds me of childhood memories

1685
01:41:15,320 --> 01:41:20,533
♪ Where everything was
    as fresh as the bright blue sky (Sky)

1686
01:41:23,244 --> 01:41:26,539
♪ Now and then, when I see her face

1687
01:41:26,664 --> 01:41:30,210
♪ She takes me away
    to that special place

1688
01:41:30,335 --> 01:41:36,341
♪ And if I stared too long,
    I'd probably break down and cry

1689
01:41:38,384 --> 01:41:43,890
♪ Woah-woah-woah
    Sweet child of mine

1690
01:41:45,975 --> 01:41:51,689
♪ Woah, oh-oh-oh
    Sweet love of mine

1691
01:42:09,374 --> 01:42:12,752
♪ She's got eyes of the bluest skies

1692
01:42:12,877 --> 01:42:16,422
♪ As if they thought of rain

1693
01:42:16,881 --> 01:42:20,385
♪ I'd hate to look into those eyes

1694
01:42:20,510 --> 01:42:23,930
♪ and see an ounce of pain

1695
01:42:24,764 --> 01:42:28,059
♪ Her hair reminds me
    of a warm, safe place

1696
01:42:28,184 --> 01:42:32,105
♪ Where as a child, I'd hide

1697
01:42:32,230 --> 01:42:34,482
♪ And pray for the thunder

1698
01:42:34,607 --> 01:42:39,612
♪ and the rain to quietly pass me by

1699
01:42:39,904 --> 01:42:45,285
♪ Woah-oh-woah
    Sweet child of mine

1700
01:42:46,536 --> 01:42:53,418
♪ Ooh-woah, oh-oh-oh
    Sweet love of mine

1701
01:43:26,451 --> 01:43:31,831
♪ Woah-oh-woah
　 　　Sweet child of mine

1702
01:43:33,166 --> 01:43:39,339
♪ Ooh-woah, oh-oh-oh
　 　　Sweet love of mine

1703
01:43:41,841 --> 01:43:47,430
♪ Woah, oh-oh-oh
　 　　Sweet child of mine

1704
01:43:47,555 --> 01:43:49,766
♪ ooh, yeah-eh

1705
01:43:49,891 --> 01:43:55,563
♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh
